c acceptance criteria.</p></header><ul class="grid gap-3 font-mono text-sm text-accent sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>Founder-led AI engineering</li><li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>ABI runtime source in Rust</li><li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>WDBX memory and retrieval source</li><li class="flex items-center gap-3"><span class="size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span>Security assertions tied to implementation scope</li></ul></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Values</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">What the company is for.</h2></header><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Safety Before Scale</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Our proposed engineering approach starts with bounded execution, explicit approvals, and failure criteria before expanding capability or throughput.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Observable Reasoning</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">We aim to expose provenance, retrieval context, decision checkpoints, and the operator actions that changed state. Each implementation needs its own evidence.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Performance With Proof</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Our evidence policy requires workload and environment notes for latency, recall, and GPU figures, and a reproduction record before calling them measured.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Private Deployment Paths</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed deployment work starts by agreeing the data boundary and evaluating on-premise, VPC, hybrid, or edge requirements.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Human-Centered Control</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">We propose visible escalation, review, and override flows, with acceptance criteria agreed by the people responsible for the system.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Research-To-Runtime Discipline</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Research translation engagements propose integration notes, constraints, and operational guidance; a prototype needs separate release acceptance.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Our mission</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Make assistant workflows inspectable.</h2></header><div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.2fr)_minmax(0,0.8fr)] lg:items-start"><p class="max-w-[66ch] text-lg leading-8 text-fg">Define the source, data boundary, tool permissions, and release evidence before expanding an assistant workflow. Research and prototypes require separate implementation and operational acceptance.</p><dl class="surface divide-y divide-border overflow-hidden"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Service scope</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Proposed</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Deployment boundary</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Agreed per project</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Evidence</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Source and qualification</span></dd></div></dl></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Principles</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Four lines we do not cross.</h2></header><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">No autonomous write action without an observable policy boundary.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">No retrieval claim without a traceable source or confidence signal.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">No benchmark without environment notes, workload shape, and reproducibility context.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">No deployment plan that ignores rollback, incident review, and human escalation.</li></ul></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Thesis</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Why on-device wins.</h2></header><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Define the data boundary</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Evaluate where a workload may run, which data may leave the operator&#x27;s environment, and which obligations need separate legal review.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Evaluate available hardware</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Inspect the target device, runtime support, and workload before proposing local inference or acceleration.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Measure the full operating cost</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Compare hardware, energy, maintenance, and provider costs using an agreed workload; local execution alone does not establish unit economics.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Entity</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Registration-level facts.</h2></header><dl class="surface divide-y divide-border overflow-hidden"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Brand</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>MLAI</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Focus</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Founder-led AI engineering</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Languages</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Rust, Swift, TypeScript</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Model</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-