ustify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Repeatable</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Figures state workload shape, hardware target, and where the number came from.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Operational</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Metrics are chosen for release decisions, not vanity dashboards.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Private-first</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Benchmark paths support local, VPC, and edge deployment constraints.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Architecture, not adjectives</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">What the active WDBX substrate implements.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">Properties verified against the active sibling Rust substrate. These are structural facts, not performance figures.</p></header><div tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable data table" class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl shadow-border focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-accent"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm" style="min-width:36rem"><thead class="bg-bg-elevated text-fg-muted"><tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Source-backed property</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">WDBX implementation</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-border bg-bg"><tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg-muted">Primary type</td><td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-fg">Vectors (ℝᵈ)</td></tr><tr><td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg-muted">Index</td><td class="px-4 py-