leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">How the runtime, memory substrate and personas fit together, and the decisions behind each boundary.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Safety drills</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Failure modes worked through in advance: what fails closed, what gets logged, and who reviews it.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Operator UX</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Control surfaces for the people running the system: calm defaults, visible state, and honest status.</p></article></div></div><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2" role="group" aria-label="Note tag"><button type="button" aria-pressed="true" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-primary text-primary-foreground">All notes</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">ENGINEERING</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">RELEASE</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">FROM ABBEY</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">RESEARCH</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">SAFETY</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">FIELD NOTE</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">PRODUCT</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">OPERATIONS</button><button type="button" aria-pressed="false" class="h-9 rounded-full px-3 font-mono text-2xs tracking-wide bg-muted text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">DEPLOYMENT</button></div><a href="/feed.xml" class="font-mono text-xs tracking-wide text-accent">RSS feed</a></div><div class="mt-6"><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-1"><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/abi-is-rust-now"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">ENGINEERING · September 29, 2026 · 3 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">ABI Is Rust Now: What Changed, and What Didn&#x27;t</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The ABI runtime moved from Zig to a nightly-Rust workspace on July 30, 2026, and WDBX became its own sibling workspace in August. Here is what that means for anyone building from source.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Research</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/wdbx-v2-release"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">RELEASE · June 9, 2026 · 7 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">WDBX V2: Observable Memory, Multimodal Inputs, and Research Alignment</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The second iteration of the WDBX runtime ships an observable pipeline: block-chain memory with temporal queries, multimodal input fusion, an async neural job queue, and a research-alignment telemetry layer that scores every turn against the constitution.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Research</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/on-saying-im-not-sure"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">FROM ABBEY · June 8, 2026 · 4 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">On Saying “I&#x27;m Not Sure”</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A note in Abbey&#x27;s voice — the empathetic-polymath persona — on why an honest “I don&#x27;t know” is one of the most useful things an agent can say.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By Abbey</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/inside-wdbx-hybrid-ranker"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">ENGINEERING · June 6, 2026 · 8 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">Inside the WDBX Hybrid Ranker: Four Factors, One Score</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Semantic similarity is only the first of four factors. Here is the exact score WDBX uses to rank retrieval candidates — and why every factor is bounded to [0,1].</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Research · WDBX Core</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/what-the-model-sees-sea"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">RESEARCH · June 4, 2026 · 7 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">How Sparse Evidence Attention Decides What the Model Sees</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Before a model reasons, something must choose which records reach the context window. SEA scores eight criteria, then packs greedily under a hard token budget.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Research · Abbey</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/weights-behind-the-personas"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">SAFETY · June 2, 2026 · 6 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">The Weights Behind Abbey, Aviva, and Abi</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Persona routing is not a hidden model call. It is a normalized weight vector with hard policy overrides and an inspectable strategy decision.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Safety Engineering</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/explainable-last-move"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">FIELD NOTE · May 21, 2026 · 7 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">Designing AI Systems That Can Explain Their Last Move</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A practical guide to capturing retrieval paths, policy checks, and operator decisions so teams can debug autonomous workflows after the fact.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Engineering</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/production-ready-agent-metrics"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">ENGINEERING · May 18, 2026 · 9 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">What We Plan to Measure Before Calling an Agent Production-Ready</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Latency and accuracy are not enough. The gate we are building tracks tool-boundary violations, source coverage, rollback paths, abstention quality, and human-review burden.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Safety Engineering</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/vector-search-to-backtrace-graphs"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">RESEARCH · May 12, 2026 · 12 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">From Vector Search to Weighted Backtrace Graphs</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Why retrieval infrastructure needs relationship-aware context and why ranking alone is not sufficient for high-stakes answer generation.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Research</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/separate-planning-review-execution"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">SAFETY · May 8, 2026 · 8 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">The Case for Separate Planning, Review, and Execution Agents</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Role separation lets teams encode checks and balances into an AI workflow instead of relying on a single agent to police itself.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Safety Engineering</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/calm-control-surfaces"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">PRODUCT · April 29, 2026 · 6 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">Making AI Control Surfaces Feel Calm Under Pressure</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Interface details that prevent overload: progressive disclosure, confidence bands, decision diffs, and emergency stop affordances.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Product</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/incident-reviews-from-ai-logs"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">OPERATIONS · April 18, 2026 · 10 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">What Incident Reviews Need From AI Logs</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">How to structure traces so teams can reconstruct context, model output, policy decisions, tool calls, and human overrides after a production event.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Operations</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/private-ai-is-not-invisible-ai"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">DEPLOYMENT · April 11, 2026 · 8 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">Private AI Does Not Mean Invisible AI</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Offline and VPC deployments still need measurable controls: local audit trails, release gates, repeatable evals, and operator-visible confidence signals.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Engineering</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/neural-backtracking"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">FIELD NOTE · February 18, 2026 · 7 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">Neural Backtracking: What a Block Chain Buys an AI Memory</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Hallucination debugging is archaeology. WDBX chains every interaction block to its parent so you can prove nobody edited the record — and so a system can be built to walk back to the exact moment a model drifted.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">By MLAI Research · WDBX Core</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/zig-016-migration"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">ENGINEERING · January 8, 2026 · 6 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">Surviving Writergate: Migrating ABI to Zig 0.16</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Zig 0.16 rebuilt std.io around vtable-based Reader and Writer interfaces. Ninety-five files later, here&#x27;s what the migration actually looked like — and the patterns we standardized on.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">Historical: the superseded Zig implementation</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/blog/why-zig"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">FIELD NOTE · November 30, 2025 · 6 min read</p><h3 class="font-display text-xl mt-1">Why WDBX Is Written in Zig</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Garbage collection pauses are invisible in the mean and fatal in the tail. WDBX is Zig because a real-time vector database is a p99 product, not a p50 product.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">Historical: the superseded Zig implementation</p></article></a></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div><div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/research"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Research</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">The longer notes with sources attached.</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/changelog"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Changelog</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">What moved, with dates.</p></a></div></div></section><script>(function(a,f){let l;try{l=JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(a)||"{}")}catch{return}const n=l?.[f||history.state?.__TSR_key];let c=!1;for(const t in n){const e=n[t],o=e?.scrollX,s=e?.scrollY;if(Number.isFinite(o)&&Number.isFinite(s)){if(t==="window")scrollTo(o,s),c=!0;else if(t)try{const r=document.querySelector(t);r&&(r.scrollLeft=o,r.scrollTop=s)}catch{}}}if(c)return;const i=location.hash.slice(1);if(i){const t=history.state?.__hashScrollIntoViewOptions??!0;if(t){const e=document.getElementById(i);e&&e.scrollIntoView(t)}return}scrollTo(0,0)})("tsr-scroll-restoration-v1_3");document.currentScript.remove()</script><!--/$--></main><footer class="mt-auto"><div class="brand-seam"></div><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-12 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 md:grid-cols-[1.4fr_2fr]"><div><a class="flex items-center gap-2.5 text-fg no-underline" aria-label="Quesar by MLAI — home" href="/"><span class="relative inline-flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-[10px] bg-bg-elevated text-accent shadow-border" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 32 32" class="size-[21px]" fill="none"><path d="M8 23 L8 10 L16 16 L24 10 L24 23" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path><circle cx="8" cy="23" r="2.6" fill="currentColor"></circle><circle cx="8" cy="10" r="2.2" fill="currentColor"></circle><circle cx="16" cy="16" r="1.9" fill="currentColor"></circle><circle cx="24" cy="10" r="2.2" fill="currentColor"></circle><circle cx="24" cy="23" r="2.6" fill="currentColor"></circle></svg></span><span class="flex flex-col leading-none"><span class="font-display text-[1.05rem] font-bold tracking-tight">Quesar</span><span class="mt-1 text-xs font-medium text-fg-subtle">by MLAI</span></span></a><p class="mt-5 max-w-sm text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">MLAI builds assistant workflows, memory systems, and developer 