d="M20.985 12.486a9 9 0 1 1-9.473-9.472c.405-.022.617.46.402.803a6 6 0 0 0 8.268 8.268c.344-.215.825-.004.803.401"></path></svg></span></button><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" class="inline-flex size-11 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-fg lg:hidden" data-overlay-trigger="menu"><span class="sr-only">Open menu</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-menu size-5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16"></path><path d="M4 12h16"></path><path d="M4 19h16"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="flex-1"><!--$--><div class="border-b border-border"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-16 pb-14 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-20"><p class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING · January 8, 2026 · 6 min read</p><h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-4xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">Surviving Writergate: Migrating ABI to Zig 0.16</h1><p class="mt-6 max-w-[62ch] text-lg leading-8 text-fg-muted">Zig 0.16 rebuilt std.io around vtable-based Reader and Writer interfaces. Ninety-five files later, here&#x27;s what the migration actually looked like — and the patterns we standardized on.</p><p class="mt-5 font-mono text-xs tracking-wide text-fg-muted">By <!-- -->MLAI Runtime Engineering</p></div></div><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><aside class="surface accent-edge p-5 [--edge:var(--accent)] mb-10 max-w-3xl"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Historical</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">This post describes the Zig implementation, which the nightly-Rust workspace replaced on July 30, 2026. It is kept for provenance, not as current build guidance.</p></aside><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Zig 0.16&#x27;s I/O overhaul — the community calls it Writergate — replaced the old generic reader/writer plumbing with explicit vtable-based std.io.Reader and std.io.Writer interfaces. For a codebase like ABI, where the database, the network layer, and the GPU pipeline all stream bytes, that change touched everything: 95 files modified before the build went green again.</p></article><article><h2 id="what-actually-broke" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">What actually broke</h2><ul class="mt-5 max-w-[66ch] space-y-3"><li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-8 text-fg"><span class="mt-3 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>Every anytype writer parameter — the old duck-typing pattern — needed an explicit interface type.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-8 text-fg"><span class="mt-3 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>Buffering moved into the caller&#x27;s hands; the new interfaces make the buffer visible instead of hiding it behind generics.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-8 text-fg"><span class="mt-3 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>Error sets narrowed. Code that relied on inferred error unions through generic writers had to name its failures.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-8 text-fg"><span class="mt-3 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>Container init churn landed at the same time: we standardized on ArrayListUnmanaged.empty and explicit allocator passing at every call site.</li></ul><div class="mt-4"><div class="min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-bg-elevated shadow-border"><div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-border px-4 py-2"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">before → after</span><button type="button" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-2 text-2xs text-fg-muted hover:bg-bg-subtle hover:text-fg"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-copy size-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="14" height="14" x="8" y="8" rx="2" ry="2"></rect><path d="M4 16c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V4c0-1.1.9-2 2-2h10c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2"></path></svg>Copy</button></div><pre tabindex="0" class="max-w-full overflow-x-auto p-5 font-mono text-xs leading-7 text-fg"><code>// 0.15 — generic duck typing
 fn serialize(self: *Block, writer: anytype) !void {
     try writer.writeAll(self.header());
 }
@@ -10,4 +10,4 @@ fn serialize(self: *Block, writer: *std.io.Writer) !void {
 zig version | grep -q &quot;0.16.0-dev&quot; || {
   echo &quot;toolchain drift: expected pinned 0.16.0-dev&quot;; exit 1;
 }
-./build.sh check</code></pre></div></div></article><article><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Ninety-five files sounds like a war story, but the honest summary is gentler: Zig&#x27;s churn is loud, shallow, and finite. The language keeps trading short-term breakage for long-term explicitness — and for a database that promises deterministic latency, explicitness is the whole brand.</p></article></div><div class="mt-14 flex max-w-3xl flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-6 border-t border-border pt-8"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm" href="/contact">Talk to our engineers</a><a class="text-right no-underline" href="/blog/why-zig"><span class="block text-xs text-fg-subtle">Next note</span><span class="mt-1 block font-display text-lg text-fg hover:underline">Why WDBX Is Written in Zig</span></a></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm active" href="/blog" data-status="active" aria-current="page">All notes</a></div><div class="mt-10"><div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><a class="s