ss="lucide lucide-moon absolute inset-0 size-4 transition-[opacity,transform,filter] duration-250 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1)] scale-100 opacity-100 blur-0" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.985 12.486a9 9 0 1 1-9.473-9.472c.405-.022.617.46.402.803a6 6 0 0 0 8.268 8.268c.344-.215.825-.004.803.401"></path></svg></span></button><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" class="inline-flex size-11 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-fg lg:hidden" data-overlay-trigger="menu"><span class="sr-only">Open menu</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-menu size-5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16"></path><path d="M4 12h16"></path><path d="M4 19h16"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="flex-1"><!--$--><div class="border-b border-border"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-16 pb-14 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-20"><p class="eyebrow">Changelog</p><h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-4xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">Milestones, not a marketing calendar.</h1><p class="mt-6 max-w-[62ch] text-lg leading-8 text-fg-muted">Versions are presentation-layer markers, not published package versions. Dates are the day the work landed. Each entry states only what the source trees implement.</p></div></div><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Current</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">The Rust tree</h2></header><ol class="grid gap-4"><li id="v0.15.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.15.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-09-29">2026-09-29</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Docs checked against their sources</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">fixed</span> — <!-- -->Every /docs article is re-checked against the ABI, WDBX and Gama READMEs and carries the date of that review.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Each article renders its own reference material (MCP tools, site surfaces, WDBX V2 downloads) from the same records as the /docs hub, so the two cannot disagree.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">fixed</span> — <!-- -->The MCP article lists all twelve contract-covered tools; WDBX V2 is described as the earlier Rust project it documents, not a Zig mirror.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.14.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.14.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-09-23">2026-09-23</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">First-party sign-in; MCP over HTTP+SSE</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->quesar.cloud leaves the Grok App Builder: sandbox tooling and platform chrome removed, bun and TypeScript throughout.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Sign-in is first-party Better Auth: email and password, passkeys, and Google, Apple or X when configured.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->abi-mcp&#x27;s optional loopback listener serves persistent MCP 2024-11-05 HTTP+SSE sessions; POST /message without a session keeps the one-shot reply. Not Streamable HTTP.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.13.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.13.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-09-22">2026-09-22</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">One site for MLAI and Quesar</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->The MLAI corporate site is merged into quesar.cloud, which becomes the only MLAI and Quesar site; the old repository is archived.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Chat audits and workspace tokens sealed with AES-256-GCM; account deletion purges per-user data.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->https://quesar.cloud serves the static build from GitHub Pages.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.12.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.12.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-09-06">2026-09-06</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Research records pinned to source</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Research publications re-reviewed against pinned ABI and WDBX commits, each with its status, limitations and review date.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.11.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.11.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-08-22">2026-08-22</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">WDBX becomes its own substrate</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->The WDBX crates are extracted from ABI into the wdbx workspace with history preserved; the abi- crate prefix is kept deliberately and ABI builds against it as a sibling.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.10.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.10.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-07-30">2026-07-30</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">ABI rewritten in Rust</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->The ABI runtime lands as a nightly-Rust workspace; the Zig tree is torn down. ./tools/check.sh is the validation gate and ./tools/cargo.sh the pinned Cargo wrapper.</li></ul></article></li></ol></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Archive</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Before the Rust rewrite</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">These entries describe the superseded Zig implementation. They are kept for provenance and are not current build or source guidance.</p></header><details class="group"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm text-accent">Show the <!-- -->9<!-- --> Zig-era entries</summary><div class="mt-6"><ol class="grid gap-4"><li id="v0.9.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.9.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-05-14">2026-05-14</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Zig 0.17-dev migration begins</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Runtime migration to Zig 0.17.0-dev started: std.process.Init entry-point pattern, argsAlloc removal, allowlist-only environString.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Framework spec pages published on the docs site, including the canonical Abbey–Aviva–Abi specification.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">fixed</span> — <!-- -->JSON-RPC envelope generation corrected in protocol tooling — responses now always emit complete closing frames.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.8.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.8.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-04-08">2026-04-08</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Abbey training pipeline</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Full Zig + MLX training stack: GQA transformer (LLaMA-style, 22 layers, 16Q/4KV heads), BPE tokenizer with fill-in-middle.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->LoRA fine-tuning, speculative decoding, sliding-window KV cache, streaming data loader, HuggingFace export, inference REPL.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->AdamW with cosine-warmup learning rate schedule standardized across training configs.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">fixed</span> — <!-- -->Known pending: mlx_value_and_grad hookup awaits a stable C gradient ABI in MLX ≥ 0.23.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.7.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.7.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-03-12">2026-03-12</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Production infrastructure expansion</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Auth, middleware, and hosted-operation work moved onto the verification roadmap instead of public claims copy.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Deployment language now separates local-first implementation from future managed-service direction.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">fixed</span> — <!-- -->Public collateral no longer presents security or disaster-recovery behavior without linked evidence.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.6.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.6.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-02-10">2026-02-10</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Performance tooling &amp; test milestone</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">perf</span> — <!-- -->SIMD CPU detection selects AVX-512 / NEON paths at startup; memory pooling and profiling hooks land in runtime/.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Evidence tracking introduced for benchmarks, source links, and verification gaps.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Scheduler and allocator language now points readers back to source-backed status.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.5.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.5.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2026-01-08">2026-01-08</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Zig 0.16 — the Writergate migration</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Migrated 95 files to the vtable-based std.io.Reader / Writer interfaces; explicit buffer ownership throughout.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Standardized ArrayListUnmanaged.empty initialization and explicit allocator passing at every call site.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->CI toolchain pinning with a fail-fast version gate mirroring build.zig.zon.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.4.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.4.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2025-12-04">2025-12-04</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">WDBX verification track</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Distributed coordination language moved from shipped-feature copy to roadmap/evidence language.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Query routing remains visible in the browser demo as a miniature, not a production cluster claim.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">perf</span> — <!-- -->Performance language now requires repeatable benchmark scripts before exact public numbers.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.3.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.3.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2025-11-06">2025-11-06</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">GPU backend matrix</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Metal, CUDA, Vulkan, WebGPU, and FPGA are presented as targets unless implementation evidence is linked.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->CPU/SIMD remains the portable baseline for public-facing language.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">perf</span> — <!-- -->Transfer and kernel speedups require source-backed measurements before publication.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.2.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.2.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2025-10-02">2025-10-02</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Storage engine core</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->HNSW approximate nearest-neighbor index tuned for cache locality.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->MVCC snapshot reads — writers never block readers; block-chained WAL for tamper-evident history.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">changed</span> — <!-- -->Security language now describes verification requirements rather than unsupported guarantees.</li></ul></article></li><li id="v0.1.0" class="scroll-mt-28"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">v0.1.0<!-- --> · <time dateTime="2025-09-10">2025-09-10</time></p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Initial public release</h3><ul class="mt-4 space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->ABI Agent + WDBX database open-sourced under Apache-2.0 — Zig core, persona scaffolding, vector storage.</li><li class="text-sm text-fg-muted"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">added</span> — <!-- -->Multi-provider LLM module: OpenAI, Anthropic, and local Ollama endpoints.</li></ul></article></li></ol></div></details></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm" href="/docs">Docs</a></div><div class="mt-10"><div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/developers"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Developers</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">The tree these milestones describe.</p></a></div></div></section><script>(function(a,f){let l;try{l=JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(a)||"{}")}catch{return}const n=l?.[f||history.state?.__TSR_key];let c=!1;for(const t in n){const e=n[t],o=e?.scrollX,s=e?.scrollY;if(Number.isFinite(o)&&Number.isFinite(s)){if(t==="window")scrollTo(o,s),