ocs</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/mcp">MCP Server</a></li></ul></div><div class="mb-6"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Operations</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/deployment">Deployment</a></li></ul></div><div class="mb-6"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Reference</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/api">Protected API</a></li></ul></div></nav><div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4"><div id="getting-started"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Start</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/getting-started">Start with the source.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Prepare an ABI checkout and follow its own validation workflow.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="architecture"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Start</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/architecture">Different tools. Clear roles.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Separate runtime, storage, interface, and application framework responsibilities.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="runtime"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Start</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/runtime">ABI runtime, as the tree actually ships.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Nightly Rust orchestration, wrappers, crates, and what a successful gate actually proves.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="trust"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Security &amp; trust</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/trust">Fail closed. Tag the figure.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Sessions, evaluation gates, and the difference between measured, reported, and target.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="evidence"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Security &amp; trust</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/evidence">Evidence before promises.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Keep documented behavior, reported testing, measured results and targets separate.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="identity"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Systems</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/identity">A companion, not a capability claim.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Understand Abbey, Aviva and ABI without confusing identity with implementation.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="gama"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Systems</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/gama">One tree. Many surfaces.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">A source-based introduction to Gama’s Swift scene and rendering model.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="personas"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/personas">Abbey, Aviva, Abi — profiles, not products.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Routing is a design mechanism. Per-persona quality is evaluated, not assumed.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="wdbx"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/wdbx">Memory is a substrate, not a chat log.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Layered HNSW, MVCC, content addressing. Integrity of storage is not truth of the record.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="wdbx-v2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/wdbx-v2">The V2 snapshot, kept for reference.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">A frozen June 2026 documentation set from the earlier Abbey WDBX project. Not the current implementation guide.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="mcp"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/mcp">Twelve contract-covered tools.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio, optional loopback HTTP. Unknown tools fail closed.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="deployment"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Operations</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/deployment">Each surface has its own gate.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Packaging orchestration, retrieval, and controls. A web check is not mobile evidence.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div id="api"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Reference</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl"><a class="text-fg no-underline hover:underline" href="/docs/api">Protected surfaces fail closed.</a></h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">The console requires a session. There is no public hosted assistant API.</p><p class="mt-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle">1<!-- --> <!-- -->min read</p></article></div><div class="mt-12 border-t border-border pt-12"><div><h2 id="reference" class="scroll-mt-28 font-display text-3xl tracking-tight">Quesar developer platform</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-7 text-fg">Build private, traceable AI workflows on the ABI runtime: retrieval provenance and hash-chained memory through WDBX, exposed over a local CLI and an MCP server. Policy-gated agents and an evaluation mesh are planned, not shipped.</p><nav aria-label="Reference sections" class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2"><a href="#ref-runtime" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-full bg-muted px-3 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:text-foreground">Runtime build</a><a href="#ref-personas" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-full bg-muted px-3 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:text-foreground">Persona routing</a><a href="#ref-wdbx" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-full bg-muted px-3 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:text-foreground">WDBX retrieval</a><a href="#ref-wdbx-v2" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-full bg-muted px-3 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:text-foreground">WDBX V2 downloads</a><a href="#ref-mcp" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-full bg-muted px-3 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:text-foreground">MCP tools</a><a href="#ref-deployment" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-full bg-muted px-3 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:text-foreground">Configuring this site</a><a href="#ref-api" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-full bg-muted px-3 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground no-underline hover:text-foreground">Site surfaces</a></nav><div class="mt-8"><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Traceable retrieval</h3></div><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-partial" title="Implemented in part. Scope is named on the page."><span aria-hidden="true">◐</span>Partial</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Index records with source metadata and inspect weighted backtrace paths and retrieval score components; snapshots and write-ahead recovery give a restore point.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Agent policy gates</h3></div><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-planned" title="Intent. Never presented as shipping."><span aria-hidden="true">○</span>Planned</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Planned: bind tools to explicit permissions, approval thresholds, and review roles before execution reaches production data. Today the MCP server only fails closed on unknown tools.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Evaluation mesh</h3></div><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-planned" title="Intent. Never presented as shipping."><span aria-hidden="true">○</span>Planned</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Planned: regression suites for retrieval faithfulness, prompt-injection resilience, latency, and operator review burden, run as a release gate.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Private runtime</h3></div><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-partial" title="Implemented in part. Scope is named on the page."><span aria-hidden="true">◐</span>Partial</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The ABI CLI and MCP server run locally on operator-owned machines. Packaging for cloud, VPC, on-premise, and offline-first deployments is the design, not a shipped installer.</p></article></div></div></div><section id="ref-runtime" aria-labelledby="ref-runtime-title" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Start</p><h3 id="ref-runtime-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">ABI runtime</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">ABI is a Rust framework for local AI orchestration, semantic vector storage, and GPU capability reporting. Build the CLI and MCP server with the repository&#x27;s pinned toolchain and the ./tools/cargo.sh wrapper.</p><div class="mt-6"><div class="min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-bg-elevated shadow-border"><div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-border px-4 