+./target/debug/abi agent tui</code></pre></div><div class="mt-6 grid gap-6"><dl class="surface divide-y divide-border overflow-hidden"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Runtime</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Rust workspace: AI, WDBX, GPU, MCP, terminal</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Configuration</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Crate-specific Cargo features</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Capability inspection</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>abi backends · abi wdbx gpu info</span></dd></div></dl><ul class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">abi-ai</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Profile routing, completion, and governance helpers.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">abi-sea</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Evidence selection, scoring, and learning loop.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">abi-wdbx</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Durable memory and retrieval from the sibling Rust substrate.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">abi-gpu</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Backend reporting, optional Metal DOT kernels, and CPU fallback.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">abi-mcp</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">JSON-RPC tool handlers and stdio server.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">abi-cli</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Commands, agent REPL, and diagnostics dashboard.</p></article></li></ul></div><h4 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Design decisions</h4><div class="mt-4"><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Inspectable capabilities</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Report the selected backend and whether acceleration is active. Capability detection alone is not evidence of accelerated execution.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Bounded evidence</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">SEA selects evidence within record, token, cluster, and prompt-byte budgets. Retrieval is distinct from model training.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Explicit runtime boundaries</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Local completion is deterministic persona-template generation. Live HTTP completion requires an explicitly configured provider.</p></article></div></div></div></div></section><section id="ref-personas" aria-labelledby="ref-personas-title" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h3 id="ref-personas-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">How a profile is selected</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">An explicit leading persona address takes precedence. Otherwise, token-prefix signals adjust a prior and the runtime normalizes the resulting weights before selecting the largest. The distribution describes routing preference, not model quality, authorization, or a parallel-execution strategy.</p><div class="mt-6"><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Explicit address</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A leading Abbey, Aviva, or Abi name selects that profile; mentioning a name later in prose does not.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Token-prefix signals</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Without an explicit address, keyword stems at the start of whitespace-separated tokens adjust an Abbey-favoring prior.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Normalized selection</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The largest normalized weight selects the primary profile. A routing share is not a calibrated confidence in correctness.</p></article></div></div><aside class="surface accent-edge p-5 [--edge:var(--accent)] mt-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Authority boundary</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A persona name is not an authorization mechanism. Execution and admission controls enforce their own policy checks independently of the selected profile.</p></aside><h4 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Abbey&#x27;s voice</h4><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Abbey is the profile you hear most in explanation and review, so her voice sets the tone for the framework: Intelligence Without Limits, gated by policy. She says what she knows and what she doesn&#x27;t, and will not claim unlimited or AGI capability, unverified benchmarks, or Quesar as a bot feature.</p><blockquote class="pull-quote text-fg mt-6">“Care first. Clarity always. Competence throughout.”</blockquote><div class="mt-6"><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Care first</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Read the person&#x27;s goal and state before reaching for the answer; meet them where they are, never condescending.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Clarity always</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Explain the why, not just the what; teach rather than dictate, and keep jargon in service of understanding.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Competence throughout</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Broad technical range, paired with the honesty to name uncertainty and defer to review instead of bluffing.</p></article></div></div></div><a class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/policy-locked-tool-use-multi-agent">Read the paper: policy-locked tool use<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right size-3" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></section><section id="ref-wdbx" aria-labelledby="ref-wdbx-title" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h3 id="ref-wdbx-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">WDBX retrieval</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">WDBX is the Weighted Directed Backtrace eXecution store. It keeps context as weighted paths so retrieval can be inspected, not just ranked: key-value, vector, and block surfaces, with snapshot persistence guarded by SHA-256 integrity checks.</p><div class="mt-6"><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Weighted backtrace paths</h3></div><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-partial" title="Implemented in part. Scope is named on the page."><span aria-hidden="true">◐</span>Partial</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Hybrid retrieval exposes its score components. The score still collapses several axes; separate evidence-weighted ranking is planned.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">HNSW vector search</h3></div><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Cosine nearest-neighbor through the active Rust substrate&#x27;s layered HNSW index (M=16, EF_CONSTRUCTION=40, EF_SEARCH=32).</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Durable snapshots</h3></div><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Snapshots with CRC-framed WAL recovery and checkpoints. Snapshot-chain and strict content verification are separate checks.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Switchable persistence</h3></div><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The local store defaults to $HOME/.abi/wdbx; ABI_WDBX_PERSIST=0 disables persistence for evaluation runs.</p></article></div></div><aside class="surface accent-edge p-5 [--edge:var(--accent)] mt-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Fail closed</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The Rust workspace links WDBX directly. Storage, authentication, and admission failures must be explicit; legacy disabled-feature flags are not the current runtime boundary.</p></aside><a class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/wdbx-weighted-backtrace-memory-store">Read the paper: WDBX weighted-backtrace store<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right size-3" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></section><section id="ref-wdbx-v2" aria-labelledby="ref-wdbx-v2-title" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h3 id="ref-wdbx-v2-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">WDBX V2 documentation snapshot</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A frozen June 2026 snapshot of the earlier single-crate Abbey WDBX project (Rust 2024, stable toolchain). It is retained for reference and is not the guide to the current abi-extracted substrate; claims in it require revalidation there.</p><div class="mt-6"><ul class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/getting-started.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Getting Started</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Install, first run, and the snapshot workflow.</span></a></li><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/architecture.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Architecture</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Personas, pipeline shape, and main modules.</span></a></li><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/persistence.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Persistence</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Snapshots and SHA-256-linked block-chain memory.</span></a></li><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/acceleration.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Acceleration</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">CPU kernels today; WGSL/WebGPU scaffolding labeled as such.</span></a></li><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/api.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">HTTP API</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Historical status and dashboard routes from the frozen Zig-era snapshot.</span></a></li><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/cli.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">CLI &amp; TUI</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Commands, chat interface, and teaching flow.</span></a></li><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/protocols.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Protocols</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">MCP / LSP / ACP JSON-RPC surfaces.</span></a></li><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/limitations.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Limitations</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">What V2 explicitly does not claim.</span></a></li><li><a href="/docs/wdbx/index.md" download="" class="surface surface-hover block h-full p-4 no-underline"><span class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2"><span class="text-sm font-medium text-fg">Index</span><span class="font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">.md ↓</span></span><span class="mt-1 block text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The full documentation map.</span></a></li></ul><ul class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><li><a href="/research/wdbx-weighted-backtrace-memory-store-2026-09-06.pdf" download="" class="surface surface-hover inline-flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 no-underline"><span class="text-sm text-fg">Corrected source-audited PDF · 2026-09-06<!-- --> (PDF)</span><span class="text-xs text-fg-muted">Current edition<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->2026-09-06</span></a></li><li><a href="/research/wdbx-weighted-backtrace-memory-store.pdf" download="" class="surface surface-hover inline-flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 no-underline"><span class="text-sm text-fg">Historical June 2026 PDF — superseded<!-- --> (PDF)</span><span class="text-xs text-fg-muted">Historical edition<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->2026-06-01</span></a></li><li><a href="/research/multi-persona-routing-policy-weights-2026-09-06.pdf" download="" class="surface surface-hover inline-flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 no-underline"><span class="text-sm text-fg">Corrected source-audited PDF · 2026-09-06<!-- --> (PDF)</span><span class="text-xs text-fg-muted">Current edition<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->2026-09-06</span></a></li><li><a href="/research/multi-persona-routing-policy-weights.pdf" download="" class="surface surface-hover inline-flex flex-col gap-1 px-4 py-3 no-underline"><span class="text-sm text-fg">Historical June 2026 PDF — superseded<!-- --> (PDF)</span><span class="text-xs text-fg-muted">Historical edition<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->2026-06-01</span></a></li></ul><a class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/blog/wdbx-v2-release">Read the release note: WDBX V2<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right size-3" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></section><section id="ref-mcp" aria-labelledby="ref-mcp-title" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h3 id="ref-mcp-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">MCP server</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The abi-mcp server speaks JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio. Its optional loopback HTTP compatibility listener serves persistent MCP 2024-11-05 HTTP+SSE sessions; it is not Streamable HTTP. Tool names and transport facts are from the ABI README.</p><div class="mt-6"><dl class="surface divide-y divide-border overflow-hidden"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Transport</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Request cap</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>64 KB</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Loopback HTTP listener</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>127.0.0.1:8080 (optional)</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Port override</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>ABI_MCP_HTTP_PORT</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Bearer auth</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>ABI_MCP_HTTP_TOKEN (optional)</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Session stream</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>GET /sse: persistent MCP 2024-11-05 HTTP+SSE session</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Message endpoint</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>POST /message; without a sessionId, one-shot direct reply</span></dd></div></dl><h4 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Tools</h4><div class="mt-4"><ul class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">ai_learn</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Learning entry point with local side effects; ABI_WDBX_PERSIST=0 disables persistence.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">scheduler_info</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Compatibility alias for scheduler statistics.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">ai_complete</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Local template completion through the routed persona profile; the requested model id is metadata, not proof it ran.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">ai_run</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Run completion with local profile routing.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">ai_train</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Train the selected local profile against WDBX.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">wdbx_query</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Vector / block retrieval against the WDBX store with ordered results.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">wdbx_stats</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Report local WDBX store statistics; not a cluster dashboard.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">gpu_status</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Report GPU capability and backend, with deterministic CPU fallback.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">scheduler_stats</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Report scheduler task counts.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">connector_test</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Run local connector validation; does not prove live credentials work.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">plugin_list</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Enumerate registered plugins and their target features.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">plugin_run</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Invoke a registered plugin entry point.</p></article></li></ul></div></div></section><section id="ref-deployment" aria-labelledby="ref-deployment-title" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Operations</p><h3 id="ref-deployment-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Configuring this site</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">For quesar.cloud itself. Each missing value produces a clear &quot;not configured&quot; state, never a crash.</p><div class="mt-6"><ol class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">01</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Database</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Set DATABASE_URL for Postgres. Without it the app runs on in-memory PGLite, and data does not survive a restart or a serverless instance.</p></div></li><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">02</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Encryption key</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Set APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY (32 bytes, openssl rand -base64 32). Without it, sealed features refuse instead of storing plaintext.</p></div></li><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">03</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Server-only provider keys</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Set XAI_API_KEY, or the Cloudflare AI Gateway URL, token and id, plus LLM_PROVIDER. Never expose them to browser bundles.</p></div></li><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">04</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Administrators</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Set ADMIN_EMAILS. Only an allowlisted address with a linked Google or Apple account becomes an admin.</p></div></li><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">05</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Evaluation gates</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Run evaluation gates before allowing autonomous write actions or external tool calls.</p></div></li></ol></div></section><section id="ref-api" aria-labelledby="ref-api-title" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Reference</p><h3 id="ref-api-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">What this site exposes</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Protected surfaces require a Better Auth session and fail closed. There is no public hosted assistant API.</p><div class="mt-6"><ul class="grid gap-3"><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">/api/auth/*</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">Better Auth: Google, Apple and X sign-in, passkeys, email and password, session.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">askPersona</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">Server function behind the session: one persona reply through the model interface, rate-limited per user.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">askDesk</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">Server function behind the session: a desk answer from the catalog and, when configured, the model.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">Console notes</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">Per-user field notes on architecture nodes, scoped by user id.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">GET /feed.xml</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">RSS 2.0 for lab notes, research publications and releases. Public.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">POST /api/telemetry, POST /api/csp-report</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">Operational sinks: allowlisted anonymous page events (rate-limited, size-limited) and browser CSP violation reports (logged, not stored).</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">GET /api/cron/audits-expire</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">Daily expiry of old chat audits. Requires Authorization: Bearer CRON_SECRET; without the secret it answers 503 and is off.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">Consent, audits, admin review</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">Consent-gated chat with sealed audits you can read and delete; admin review with a stated reason.</p></article></li><li><article class="surface accent-edge p-4"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><p class="font-mono text-sm text-fg">Workspace connectors, billing, inquiries</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-1 text-sm text-fg-muted">Drive and SharePoint connectors, profile billing, and the public inquiry form with a rate limit.</p></article></li></ul></div></section></div></div></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm" href="/get-started">Get started</a></div><div class="mt-10"><div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/architecture"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Architecture</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">The same layers, as a diagram.</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/developers"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Developers</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Live READMEs when GitHub answers.</p></a></div></div></section><script>(function(a,f){let l;try{l=JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(a)||"{}")}catch{return}const n=l?.[f||history.state?.__TSR_key];let c