ems-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/runtime">ABI Runtime</a></li></ul></div><div class="mb-6"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Security &amp; trust</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/trust">Security &amp; trust</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/evidence">Evidence</a></li></ul></div><div class="mb-6"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Systems</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/identity">Identity</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/gama">Gama</a></li></ul></div><div class="mb-6"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Architecture</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a aria-current="page" class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors bg-primary/10 text-fg active" href="/docs/personas" data-status="active">Persona Routing</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/wdbx">WDBX Retrieval</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/wdbx-v2">WDBX V2 Docs</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/mcp">MCP Server</a></li></ul></div><div class="mb-6"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Operations</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/deployment">Deployment</a></li></ul></div><div class="mb-6"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Reference</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/api">Protected API</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="three-voices-one-substrate" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Three voices, one substrate</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Abbey is care: empathetic, scaffolded. Aviva is clarity: concise, unfiltered. Abi is competence: the adaptive moderator that scores the blend. They are interaction roles, not separately deployed commercial services.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Product ABI is violet. Persona Abi is cyan. Mixing those identities is how a page starts claiming three products that do not exist.</p></article><article><h2 id="what-the-demo-is" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">What the demo is</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The in-browser persona router is an illustrative keyword-sentiment heuristic. The inspected local router uses deterministic rules. This is not evidence of a trained classifier, and it is not a hosted Abbey session.</p><p class="mt-5 max-w-[66ch] border-l-2 border-primary/50 bg-muted/50 px-4 py-3 text-base leading-7 text-fg">Open /demo to watch α, or /abbey-bot for a companion thread that stays in this browser.</p></article><ul class="mt-8 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Abbey identity specification</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">Further reading linked by the ABI README; not separately audited here.</p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">ABI README</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">Source description, tool commands and stated limitations; not a reproduced test run.</p></li></ul><p class="mt-4 text-xs text-fg-subtle">Checked against these sources on<!-- --> <time dateTime="2026-09-29">2026-09-29</time>.</p></div><section id="how-a-profile-is-selected" aria-labelledby="how-a-profile-is-selected-title" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-28"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Architecture</p><h2 id="how-a-profile-is-selected-title" class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">How a profile is selected</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">An explicit leading persona address takes precedence. Otherwise, token-prefix signals adjust a prior and the runtime normalizes the resulting weights before selecting the largest. The distribution describes routing preference, not model quality, authorization, or a parallel-execution strategy.</p><div class="mt-6"><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Explicit address</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A leading Abbey, Aviva, or Abi name selects that profile; mentioning a name later in prose does not.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Token-prefix signals</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Without an explicit address, keyword stems at the start of whitespace-separated tokens adjust an Abbey-favoring prior.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Normalized selection</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The largest normalized weight selects the primary profile. A routing share is not a calibrated confidence in correctness.</p></article></div></div><aside class="surface accent-edge p-5 [--edge:var(--accent)] mt-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Authority boundary</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A persona name is not an authorization mechanism. Execution and admission controls enforce their own policy checks independently of the selected profile.</p></aside><h3 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Abbey&#x27;s voice</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Abbey is the profile you hear most in explanation and review, so her voice sets the tone for the framework: Intelligence Without Limits, gated by policy. She says what she knows and what she doesn&#x27;t, and will not claim unlimited or AGI capability, unverified benchmarks, or Quesar as a bot feature.</p><blockquote class="pull-quote text-fg mt-6">“Care first. Clarity always. Competence throughout.”</blockquote><div class="mt-6"><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3"><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Care first</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Read the person&#x27;s goal and state before reaching for the answer; meet them where they are, never condescending.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Clarity always</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Explain the why, not just the what; teach rather than dictate, and keep jargon in service of understanding.</p></article></div><div><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 h-full"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Competence throughout</h3></div></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Broad technical range, paired with the honesty to name uncertainty and defer to review instead of bluffing.</p></article></div></div></div><a class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/policy-locked-tool-use-multi-agent">Read the paper: policy-locked tool use<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right size-3" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div></section><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent active" href="/docs" data-status="active" aria-current="page">All docs</a><a class="text-fg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/gama">Previous: One tree. Many surfaces.</a><a class="text-fg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/wdbx">Next: Memory is a substrate, not a chat log.</a></div></div><nav aria-label="On this page" class="mt-8 hidden xl:block"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">On this page</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-1"><li><a href="#three-voices-one-substrate" class="text-sm text-fg-muted no-underline hover:text-fg">Three voices, one substrate</a></li><li><a href="#what-the-demo-is" class="text-sm text-fg-muted no-underline hover:text-fg">What the demo is</a></li><li><a href="#how-a-profile-is-selected" class="text-sm text-fg-muted no-underline hover:text-fg">How a profile is selected</a></li></ul></nav></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[backgrou