s="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/deployment">Deployment</a></li></ul></div><div class="mb-6"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Reference</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/docs/api">Protected API</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="operator-owned-by-default" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Operator-owned by default</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Remote providers are optional and credential-gated. This website does not see your documents, weights, or generated output from your own ABI runtime. Unknown MCP tools fail closed in that runtime.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A green web check is not mobile evidence. A reported test suite is not an independently reproduced benchmark.</p></article><article><h2 id="what-signing-in-to-this-site-does" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">What signing in to this site does</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Sign-in is first-party Better Auth: email and password, passkeys, and Google, Apple or X when their credentials are configured. It opens the console, which holds your field notes, a consent-gated model chat, and the audits of those chats. It is not an Abbey session and not a hosted WDBX store.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Chat audits and workspace refresh tokens are sealed with AES-256-GCM under a server key. Without that key those features refuse rather than store plaintext. You can read and delete your audits, and deleting your account removes your per-user rows.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Administrators are an email allowlist plus a linked Google or Apple account. An allowlisted email-and-password account is refused, because sign-up is open and unverified.</p></article><article><h2 id="provenance-language" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Provenance language</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Figures on this site are tagged measured, target, or reported. A new number ships only with the source that produced it. Planned is never shipping. Research is not a Quesar product claim.</p><ul class="mt-5 max-w-[66ch] space-y-3"><li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-8 text-fg"><span class="mt-3 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>Measured — produced by a repository test or documented artifact</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-8 text-fg"><span class="mt-3 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>Reported — stated by source, not rerun here</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-base leading-8 text-fg"><span class="mt-3 size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>Target — intent, never presented as current performance</li></ul></article><ul class="mt-8 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">External claims audit</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">Further reading linked by the ABI README; not separately audited here.</p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/developers">quesar.cloud repository rules</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">This site&#x27;s own auth, admin, encryption and configuration decisions.</p></li></ul><p class="mt-4 text-xs text-fg-subtle">Checked against these sources on<!-- --> <time dateTime="2026-09-29">2026-09-29</time>.</p></div><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a c