ass="sr-only">parent</span> <!-- -->3e9f<!-- --> <span class="sr-only">, via <!-- -->Abbey</span></p></div></li></ol></div><figcaption class="border-t border-border px-5 py-3 text-xs text-fg-subtle sm:px-6">Illustrative trace. Bar length is the retrieval weight; each block names its parent hash.</figcaption></figure><a class="mt-5 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-accent" href="/docs/wdbx">Read the WDBX guide →</a></div></div></section><section id="developers" aria-labelledby="developers-title" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-border"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10"><header class="lg:col-span-5"><p class="eyebrow">For builders</p><h2 id="developers-title" class="section-title mt-4">Start with the source.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-[52ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Explore ABI’s Rust framework, local CLI, and MCP contracts. Follow the setup and verification guidance before connecting models, tools, or memory.</p></header><div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-7"><div class="vision-code rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-5 sm:p-7"><p class="mb-5 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">Local CLI example — requires ABI source setup</p><pre class="overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-7"><code>./tools/cargo.sh build -p abi-cli
-./target/debug/abi agent plan &quot;stage a safe WDBX refactor&quot;</code></pre></div><p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Local framework and contracts. Hosted Quesar APIs and platform SDKs are not published.</p><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2"><a class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-accent" href="/developers">Read the developer path →</a><a class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-accent" href="/docs/getting-started">Open setup guide →</a></div></div></div></section><section id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-border"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10"><header class="lg:col-span-5"><p class="eyebrow">Research and simulation</p><h2 id="research-title" class="section-title mt-4">Explore the ideas. Inspect the evidence.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-[52ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Read source-backed work on memory, retrieval, model orchestration, and provenance, with implementation status beside the research.</p></header><div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-7"><div class="border-t border-border pt-6"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-partial" title="Actively changing. Do not treat as stable."><span aria-hidden="true">◦</span>In development</span><h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl">NYON: deterministic worlds</h3><p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A Rust strategy game with a separate offline Galaxy Workshop sandbox.</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-subtle">Workshop development and desktop/browser qualification remain in progress. NYON is a related source project.</p><a class="mt-5 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-accent" href="/source/nyon">Explore NYON’s source →</a></div><a class="mt-4 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-accent" href="/research">Visit the research library →</a></div></div></section><section id="engagements" aria-labelledby="engagements-title" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-border"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24"><header class="max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">For organizations · Services</p><h2 id="engagements-title" class="section-title mt-4">Choose the next engineering decision.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-[52ch] text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Define a private AI engagement around retrieval, tool permissions, deployment topology, and evaluation. Scope and acceptance criteria are agreed for each project.</p></header><div class="min-w-0"><div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3"><article class="border-t border-border pt-6"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-planned" title="Intent. Never presented as shipping."><span aria-hidden="true">○</span>Planned</span><h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl">Assess the system</h3><p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Scope an audit of workflows, data paths, and approval gates. Use workshops and runtime profiling to turn open questions into a risk register, architecture decisions, and an optimization backlog.</p><ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted"><li>Autonomy Readiness Audit</li><li>Executive &amp; Engineering Workshops</li><li>Model &amp; Runtime Optimization</li></ul><a class="mt-6 inline-block text-accent" href="/services">Explore services →</a></article><article class="border-t border-border pt-6"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-planned" title="Intent. Never presented as shipping."><span aria-hidden="true">○</span>Planned</span><h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl">Build a bounded workflow</h3><p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Scope retrieval architecture, agent roles, and deployment topology. Translate research into an API contract and test plan, with the data boundary and tool permissions defined before implementation.</p><ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted"><li>WDBX Retrieval Architecture</li><li>Multi-Agent Orchestration</li><li>Private AI Deployment</li><li>Research Translation</li></ul><a class="mt-6 inline-block text-accent" href="/services">Explore services →</a></article><article class="border-t border-border pt-6"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-planned" title="Intent. Never presented as shipping."><span aria-hidden="true">○</span>Planned</span><h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl">Harden the release path</h3><p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Scope policy checks, audit events, red-team scenarios, and regression evaluation. Agree on release gates and a rollback plan before expanding autonomy.</p><ul class="mt-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-fg-muted"><li>Safety &amp; Compliance Layering</li><li>Continuous Evaluation Systems</li></ul><a class="mt-6 inline-block text-accent" href="/services">Explore services →</a></article></div></div></div></section><section id="evidence" aria-labelledby="evidence-title" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-border"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10"><header class="lg:col-span-5"><p class="eyebrow">Evidence</p><h2 id="evidence-title" class="section-title mt-4">Inspect the work before choosing a path.</h2></header><div class="min-w-0 lg:col-span-7"><ul class="divide-y divide-border border-y border-border"><li class="py-5"><a class="font-display text-xl text-accent" href="/architecture">Inspect the architecture</a><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Read the runtime layers alongside their implementation limits.</p></li><li class="py-5"><a class="font-display text-xl text-accent" href="/developers">Read the source</a><p class="mt-2 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Follow repository links and setup guidance for a technical review.</p></li><li class="py-5"><a class="font-display text-xl text-accent"