on class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><p class="max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The trace and private runtime capabilities are partial; the control plane is in development and the evaluation mesh is planned. Read each status before choosing an integration.</p><a href="https://github.com/donaldfilimon/quesar.cloud/blob/f3ccc082f72ef868ca3c3a60f332f7efe9cfe492/src/lib/mlai/categories/platform.ts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Inspect the source behind this page</a></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Stack</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Bottom to top.</h2></header><div class="mb-10"><div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.05fr)_minmax(0,0.95fr)] lg:items-center"><div role="radiogroup" aria-required="false" dir="ltr" class="chip-stack relative mx-auto grid w-full max-w-lg gap-0" aria-label="Stack layers" tabindex="-1" style="outline:none"><span class="absolute top-3 bottom-3 left-3 w-px bg-accent/40" aria-hidden="true"></span><button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-state="unchecked" value="abbey" class="items-center text-sm text-fg-muted hover:text-fg data-[state=checked]:bg-bg-subtle data-[state=checked]:text-fg chip-slab accent-edge relative block h-auto w-full rounded-3xl px-6 py-5 text-left [--edge:var(--abbey)] shadow-border bg-bg-elevated/80" style="margin-top:0;z-index:3" tabindex="-1" data-radix-collection-item=""><span class="absolute top-1/2 left-[-0.55rem] size-2 -translate-y-1/2 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">01<!-- --> · <!-- -->Application</span><span class="mt-1 block font-display text-2xl tracking-tight text-fg">Abbey</span></button><input type="radio" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" style="position:absolute;pointer-events:none;opacity:0;margin:0;transform:translateX(-100%)" value="abbey"/><button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="true" data-state="checked" value="abi" class="items-center text-sm text-fg-muted hover:text-fg data-[state=checked]:bg-bg-subtle data-[state=checked]:text-fg chip-slab accent-edge relative block h-auto w-full rounded-3xl px-6 py-5 text-left [--edge:var(--abi)] shadow-border-hover bg-bg-elevated" style="margin-top:-8px;z-index:2" tabindex="-1" data-radix-collection-item=""><span class="absolute top-1/2 left-[-0.55rem] size-2 -translate-y-1/2 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">02<!-- --> · <!-- -->Compute</span><span class="mt-1 block font-display text-2xl tracking-tight text-fg">ABI</span></button><input type="radio" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" style="position:absolute;pointer-events:none;opacity:0;margin:0;transform:translateX(-100%)" checked="" value="abi"/><button type="button" role="radio" aria-checked="false" data-state="unchecked" value="wdbx" class="items-center text-sm text-fg-muted hover:text-fg data-[state=checked]:bg-bg-subtle data-[state=checked]:text-fg chip-slab accent-edge relative block h-auto w-full rounded-3xl px-6 py-5 text-left [--edge:var(--wdbx)] shadow-border bg-bg-elevated/80" style="margin-top:-8px;z-index:1" tabindex="-1" data-radix-collection-item=""><span class="absolute top-1/2 left-[-0.55rem] size-2 -translate-y-1/2 rounded-full bg-accent" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">03<!-- --> · <!-- -->Storage</span><span class="mt-1 block font-display text-2xl tracking-tight text-fg">WDBX</span></button><input type="radio" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" style="position:absolute;pointer-events:none;opacity:0;margin:0;transform:translateX(-100%)" value="wdbx"/></div><div><p class="text-xs text-accent">Compute</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-3xl tracking-tight">ABI</h3><p class="mt-3 max-w-sm text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Reasoning, routing, orchestration. Inspectable context.</p><a class="mt-5 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Open <!-- -->ABI</a></div></div></div><div class="grid gap-4"><a class="no-underline" href="/wdbx"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover [--edge:var(--wdbx)] grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-[8rem_1fr] sm:items-baseline"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Storage</p><div><h3 class="font-display text-2xl">WDBX</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Episodic substrate: durable records, vector retrieval, causal history, and structural provenance.</p></div></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/abi"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover [--edge:var(--abi)] grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-[8rem_1fr] sm:items-baseline"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Compute</p><div><h3 class="font-display text-2xl">ABI</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Deterministic persona routing, template completion, and source-defined tools.</p></div></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/abbey"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover [--edge:var(--abbey)] grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-[8rem_1fr] sm:items-baseline"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Application</p><div><h3 class="font-display text-2xl">Abbey</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Assistant source: persona profiles, capability ledger, and local CLI.</p></div></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/quesar"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover [--edge:var(--accent)] grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-[8rem_1fr] sm:items-baseline"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Product</p><div><h3 class="font-display text-2xl">Quesar</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Experimental local website builder: browser client, paired operator-owned service, and separately configured model provider.</p></div></article></a></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">This checkout</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Independent gates. One repository.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">quesar.cloud is the current site and contains the local service clients, sidecars, and native shell. Each needs its own verification; a green web gate does not prove device behavior.</p></header><div tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable data table" class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl shadow-border focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-accent"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm" style="min-width:36rem"><thead class="bg-bg-elevated text-fg-muted"><tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Path</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Purpose</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-medium">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-border bg-bg"><tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">src/</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg-muted">The one app: TanStack Start site, console, admin, workspace, demos, Quasar screens, and cinematic showcase</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></td></tr><tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">migrations/</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg-muted">Postgres schema (Neon, or in-memory PGLite without DATABASE_URL): auth, notes, audits, connectors, rate limits</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></td></tr><tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">sidecars/quasar-service/</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg-muted">Local AI site-builder service (Bun, port 4700) that the /quasar screens drive; run it yourself, never hosted</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-partial" title="Runnable or inspectable, not a product claim."><span aria-hidden="true">◌</span>Experimental</span></td></tr><tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">sidecars/python-worker/</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg-muted">Optional local document extraction and embeddings worker, reached by URL, never spawned</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-partial" title="Runnable or inspectable, not a product claim."><span aria-hidden="true">◌</span>Experimental</span></td></tr><tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">native/</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg-muted">Capacitor shell source that loads the deployed site, with an Android project and a CloudKit availability plugin</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-partial" title="Implemented in part. Scope is named on the page."><span aria-hidden="true">◐</span>Partial</span></td></tr><tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs">notes/</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-fg-muted">Merge spec, plan and gap matrix, plus the pre-merge MLAI records under notes/mlai/ (docs/ holds the built static site)</td><td class="px-4 py-3"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Personas vs products</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Two color axes. Do not mix them.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">Product accents: WDBX cyan, ABI violet, Abbey emerald. Persona colors: Abbey emerald, Aviva violet, Abi cyan. The ABI product is violet; the Abi persona is cyan.</p></header><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3"><article class="surface accent-edge [--edge:var(--abbey)] p-7"><h3 class="flex items-center gap-2.5 font-display text-2xl"><span class="size-2.5 rounded-full bg-persona-abbey" aria-hidden="true"></span>Abbey</h3><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-subtle">Empathic polymath</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">High-EQ tutor and partner. Scaffolds, names uncertainty, and keeps the human in the loop.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge [--edge:var(--aviva)] p-7"><h3 class="flex items-center gap-2.5 font-display text-2xl"><span class="size-2.5 rounded-full bg-persona-aviva" aria-hidden="true"></span>Aviva</h3><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-subtle">Unfiltered expert</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Direct, concise, unhedged. Fewer tokens by design. Facts without preamble.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge [--edge:var(--wdbx)] p-7"><h3 class="flex items-center gap-2.5 font-display text-2xl"><span class="size-2.5 rounded-full bg-persona-abi" aria-hidden="true"></span>Abi</h3><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-subtle">Adaptive moderator</p><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Routes and blends. Classifies intent, applies policy, and reports what the ledger can prove.</p></article></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Configuration</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">What the active crate actually sets.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">Sourced from the Rust substrate. Not a scoreboard.</p></header><dl class="surface divide-y divide-border overflow-hidden"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Engine</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Layered HNSW</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Concurrency</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>MVCC</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">M</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>16</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">efConstruction</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>40</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">efSearch</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>32</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Metric</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Cosine</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Addressing</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Content-addressed</span></dd></div><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3 px-5 py-3"><dt class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">Sharding</dt><dd class="flex items-center gap-2 font-mono text-sm text-fg tabular"><span>Not established</span></dd></div></dl></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Related</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Gama is not Quesar.</h2></header><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Gama</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A modular declarative Swift UI framework with TUI, Apple, WebAssembly, and embed backends. It lives at<!-- --> <a class="text-accent underline underline-offset-4" href="/gama">Gama</a>. It is not a Quesar product, not an Abbey runtime, and not evidence of a shipped spatial engine.</p></article></section><section id="control-plane" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28 scroll-mt-32"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Trust boundary</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Configured console Chat: three boundaries.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">The server-side console Chat path checks identity, provider configuration, and audit storage within one request. Broader runtime control-plane work has separate status and acceptance requirements.</p></header><div class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-3"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abi)] h-full"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span><h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl">Account-scoped access</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Protected console functions use Better Auth sessions and scope per-user records by user id. Admin access requires an allowlisted email and a linked Google or Apple account. Public inquiry and configuration functions have separate controls.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abbey)] h-full"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span><h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl">One server-side model interface</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Website model requests use a server-side interface configured for xAI or Cloudflare AI Gateway to Gemini. Console Chat checks provider availability and a per-user rate limit; the request builder does not automatically add account email. Provider and deployment acceptance require separate evidence.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--wdbx)] h-full"><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span><h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-xl">Records you control</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Conversation audits and workspace refresh tokens are sealed with AES-256-GCM under APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY, bound to their owner and purpose. Console Chat requires current audit consent and stores its sealed exchange before returning a reply. Contact inquiry fields are stored separately and are not covered by this application-level sealing.</p></article></div></section><section id="request-path" aria-labelledby="request-path-heading" class="scroll-mt-32 border-y border-border"><div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.72fr)_minmax(0,1.28fr)] lg:items-start"><div class="min-w-0 lg:sticky lg:top-32"><p class="eyebrow">One request</p><h2 id="request-path-heading" class="section-title mt-4">Five checks for console Chat.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">In the configured server console Chat path, authenticate, consent, generate, encrypt, and store the audit before returning the reply. These checks are implemented in source. The static preview has no server chat, and live deployment acceptance requires separate evidence.</p><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px border-border bg-card/80 text-foreground hover:bg-muted h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm mt-7" href="/security">Inspect the security model <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right size-4" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></a></div><ol class="grid min-w-0 gap-3"><li class="surface grid gap-3 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_minmax(0,1fr)]"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">01</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Authenticate</h3><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">The protected console Chat function requires a Better Auth session and uses that user&#x27;s id. This requirement does not apply to every public server function.</p></div></li><li class="surface grid gap-3 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_minmax(0,1fr)]"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">02</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Consent</h3><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Console Chat requires acceptance of the current audit policy before its provider request. Other website features have their own data and permission boundaries.</p></div></li><li class="surface grid gap-3 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_minmax(0,1fr)]"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">03</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Generate</h3><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Console Chat requires a configured provider and checks a per-user rate limit before generation. The server request does not automatically include account email.</p></div></li><li class="surface grid gap-3 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_minmax(0,1fr)]"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">04</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Encrypt</h3><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Console Chat refuses without a valid audit-encryption key. Its prompt and reply are sealed with AES-256-GCM, bound to the audit owner.</p></div></li><li class="surface grid gap-3 p-5 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_minmax(0,1fr)]"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">05</span><div class="min-w-0"><div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Commit</h3><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-medium text-status-current" title="Present in public source and used as described."><span aria-hidden="true">●</span>Current</span></div><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Console Chat stores the sealed audit before returning a successful reply. If audit storage fails, the generated reply is withheld.</p></div></li></ol></div></section><section id="product-boundary" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28 scroll-mt-20"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Product boundary</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">An experimental local builder.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">The Quasar browser client pairs with an operator-owned service that scaffolds Next.js projects and uses a configured provider for generation. Live provider generation remains unverified. ABI, WDBX, and Abbey have separate source and integration boundaries.</p></header><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">What it is</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Quesar&#x27;s available source surface is the experimental Quasar website builder: a browser client paired to a separately running operator-owned service. Generation uses a configured provider; live provider acceptance remains unverified.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Separate acceptance boundaries</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Builder source does not establish a trained Quesar foundation model, a hosted Abbey product session, compliance certification, or a performance result. The configured website console is a separate model-request path.</p></article></div><div class="mt-12"><p class="eyebrow">Docs</p><h3 class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Start with the trust boundary.</h3><div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-3"><a class="no-underline" href="/docs/getting-started"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover flex h-full min-h-44 flex-col"><h4 class="font-display text-xl text-fg">Getting started</h4><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Console entry, what a scoped evaluation requires, and where setup lives.</p><span class="mt-auto pt-5 text-sm text-accent">Open →</span></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/security"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover flex h-full min-h-44 flex-col"><h4 class="font-display text-xl text-fg">Security &amp; trust</h4><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Identity, provider boundary, sealing, retention, and disclosure.</p><span class="mt-auto pt-5 text-sm text-accent">Open →</span></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/docs/architecture"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover flex h-full min-h-44 flex-col"><h4 class="font-display text-xl text-fg">Architecture</h4><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Control-plane framing and the inspectable WDBX substrate: facts, not a scoreboard.</p><span class="mt-auto pt-5 text-sm text-accent">Open →</span></article></a></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm" href="/contact">Discuss your project</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px border-border bg-card/80 text-foreground hover:bg-muted h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm" href="/architecture">Architecture</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outli