 fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-menu size-5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16"></path><path d="M4 12h16"></path><path d="M4 19h16"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="flex-1"><!--$--><div class="border-b border-border"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-16 pb-14 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-20"><p class="eyebrow">Browser document preview</p><h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-4xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">Abbey</h1><p class="mt-6 max-w-[62ch] text-lg leading-8 text-fg-muted">Explore a browser document workspace and its optional configured server model-request path.</p></div></div><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Availability</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">What you can use today</h2></header><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">Browser document preview</p><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">Documents are stored in this browser&#x27;s localStorage. This preview does not establish setup or acceptance for a separate Abbey app.</p></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Setup</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Prepare your environment</h2></header><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">A browser. A configured server and model provider are required for model requests; the static preview cannot call a model.</p></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Design context</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Read the design alongside the evidence</h2></header><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">The following equations, persona descriptions and interactive demonstrations explain design intent. They do not establish trained-model quality, general safety, emotional understanding or implementation beyond the availability stated above. Follow the research links for source-backed status and limitations. The local Abbey document workspace and the ABI persona design are separate integration surfaces.</p></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Specialty</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Human-centric qualities in technical discourse</h2></header><div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abbey)] flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Persona routing</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Routes each turn through Abbey, Aviva, or Abi with an inspectable reason — so the voice matches the job and the handoff is a trace event, not a guess.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abbey)] flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Durable memory</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Remembers facts and channel context with permission, on namespace-scoped stores you can inspect — rapport without opaque black-box recall.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abbey)] flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Ops with guardrails</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Calm ops help that names uncertainty, defers when policy says so, and never claims unlimited capability, AGI, unverified benchmarks, or NYX/Quesar as bot features.</p></article></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">The Abbey cognitive loop</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">How empathy is operationalized</h2></header><div class="mt-6"><div><article class="truth-row"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">01</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Sentiment &amp; frustration detection</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">Input from Abi is evaluated for emotional state, prior knowledge, and subject complexity. A high frustration score triggers the Scaffolding Protocol.</p></div></article><article class="truth-row"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">02</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">The Scaffolding Protocol</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">A tiered explanation: a high-level metaphor first → the precise technical answer → suggested pathways for deeper exploration.</p></div></article><article class="truth-row"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">03</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Metaphorical Mapping Engine</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">Finds the most conceptually parallel non-technical domain (e.g. music theory for distributed systems). Measured by conceptual isomorphism — structural similarity, not factual overlap.</p></div></article><article class="truth-row"><span class="font-mono text-sm text-accent">04</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-2xl tracking-tight">Dynamic visual aid</h3><p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">The mapping becomes a generative-image prompt, producing a visual anchor that encapsulates the core concept.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Operational pillars</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">What sets Abbey apart</h2></header><div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abbey)] flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Confident &amp; theoretical</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Encouraged to form and share well-reasoned opinions and engage &#x27;what-if&#x27; ideas — human-like, not merely a fact reporter.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abbey)] flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Unwavering technical rigor</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Meticulous code analysis and completion with validation in the loop, so answers are checked rather than assumed.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abbey)] flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Perpetual student</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Designed to research live sources when a query exceeds internal knowledge, and to validate sources before responding.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 [--edge:var(--abbey)] flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Deep personalization</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Recalls and synthesizes prior conversations (with permission) to build genuine, long-term rapport.</p></article></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Foundation</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Backed by WDBX</h2></header><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-base">Abbey&#x27;s memory and persona voices ride on WDBX. Per-channel vectors are stored with namespace-scoped isolation, and persona-token injection dynamically shapes the shared core into Abbey, Aviva, or Abi — designed so switching voices carries no reload cost, preserving the responsiveness a real-time partner demands.</p></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Next</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Keep going.</h2></header><div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/workspace"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Setup documentation</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">A browser. A configured server and model provider are required for model requests; the static preview cannot call a model.</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/research/ai-overview"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">AI &amp; agent behavior</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Read the supporting research and its limitations.</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/research/tui-overview"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">TUI &amp; operator tools</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Read the supporting research and its limitations.</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/get-started"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Get started</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Choose your next step.</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/products/abi"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">ABI</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Local developer framework</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/products/wdbx"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">WDBX</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Implemented Rust components for local integration</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/products/quasar"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Quasar</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Experimental local website builder with a browser cli