a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/sparse-evidence-attention-context-assembly">Sparse Evidence Attention for Bounded Context Assembly</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/backtrace-confidence-signals-hallucination">Backtrace Confidence Signals for Hallucination Reduction</a></li><li><a aria-current="page" class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors bg-primary/10 text-fg active" href="/research/chunk-provenance-long-context-retrieval" data-status="active">Chunk Provenance in Long-Context Retrieval Systems</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">GPU &amp; compute</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/gpu-overview">GPU &amp; compute</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/latency-budgets-real-time-orchestration">Latency Budgets for Real-Time AI Orchestration</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/gpu-implementation-guide">Evaluating Metal acceleration and CPU fallback</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">MCP integrations</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-overview">MCP integrations</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-implementation-guide">Connecting an MCP client to ABI</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">TUI &amp; operator tools</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-overview">TUI &amp; operator tools</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-implementation-guide">Using the local diagnostics dashboard and agent REPL</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-6"><a class="text-xs text-fg-subtle no-underline hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations">Implementations</a><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="mb-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Practical summary</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Prototype project recall or document assistance without placing every available record in a prompt.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Status</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">This is a proposed study or application pattern, not a completed experiment or deployed feature.</p><p class="mt-2 font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">Reviewed <!-- -->2026-09-30</p></article></div><nav aria-label="Related products" class="mb-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent" href="/products">All products</a></nav><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="practical-context" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Practical context</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A proposed application pattern for preserving source references through document retrieval.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Prototype project recall or document assistance without placing every available record in a prompt.</p></article><article><h2 id="implementation-and-research-boundary" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Implementation and research boundary</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A document application can retain source identity and segment boundaries alongside retrieved content, then present those references with an answer. The evidence path reads metadata from durable records and assembles bounded snippets.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Enduring citation resolution also requires versioned source retention and an application-level resolver. Those requirements are proposed here; the presence of storage metadata does not prove long-term citation validity or regulatory compliance.</p></article><article><h2 id="a-proposed-record-model" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">A proposed record model</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Bind each retrievable segment to a source identifier, a source version and a reproducible boundary such as a byte range or stable structural anchor. Keep the original text available under an authorized retention policy. A citation should resolve to that specific version rather than whatever content happens to be at the source URL today. The inspected evidence path consumes metadata and snippets, but the full document-version resolver described here belongs to an application and is proposed.</p></article><article><h2 id="data-flow-and-drift-handling" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Data flow and drift handling</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">At ingestion, record how the document was parsed and segmented. Carry the segment identifier through candidate retrieval, selection and answer presentation. When a source changes, distinguish an updated version from an in-place replacement that would invalidate old references. A hash can detect content change but does not grant permission to retain or reveal the document. On deletion, define how the product explains an unavailable reference while respecting the owner’s retention and access rules.</p></article><article><h2 id="proposed-validation-fixtures" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Proposed validation fixtures</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Use documents with repeated passages, changed headings, reordered sections and identical text in different sources. Ask queries that retrieve each case, then verify that displayed references resolve to the intended version and boundaries. Include a removed source and an unauthorized reader so that unavailable evidence is handled explicitly. Test the resolver independently of answer quality, then evaluate whether the answer actually supports its claims with those segments. Long context is not a substitute for citation correctness, and this design is not a certification of compliance.</p></article><article><h2 id="evaluation-before-adoption" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Evaluation before adoption</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Use a documented corpus with relevant, irrelevant, conflicting and missing evidence. Review selected context and bounded behavior alongside answer quality; a successful selection test alone is not a hallucination-reduction result.</p></article></div><h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Limitations</h3><div class="mt-3"><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Token costs are estimates; the implementation also enforces a prompt-byte boundary.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Scoring heuristics do not guarantee relevance, truth or improved answer quality.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Enduring citation resolution also requires versioned source retention and an application-level resolver. Those requirements are proposed here; the presence of storage metadata does not prove long-term citation validity or regulatory compliance.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Supporting sources</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Bounded evidence recall and prompt assembly</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Durable store and writer ownership</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li></ul></div></div><div class="mt-12 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">More on this track</h3><ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/sea-overview">SEA evidence selection</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/sparse-evidence-attention-context-assembly">Sparse Evidence Attention for Bounded Context Assembly</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/backtrace-confidence-signals-hallucination">Backtrace Confidence Signals for Hallucination Reduction</a></li></ul></div><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Nested implementations</h3><ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hov