class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-overview">TUI &amp; operator tools</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-implementation-guide">Using the local diagnostics dashboard and agent REPL</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-6"><a class="text-xs text-fg-subtle no-underline hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations">Implementations</a><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="mb-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Practical summary</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Assess whether a target Apple workstation can use the optional Metal DOT path.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Status</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">The documented local interface exists in the cited source. Actual runtime and client acceptance must be checked in the intended environment.</p><p class="mt-2 font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">Reviewed <!-- -->2026-09-30</p></article></div><nav aria-label="Related products" class="mb-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent" href="/products">All products</a></nav><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="start-with-the-intended-workflow" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Start with the intended workflow</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Assess whether a target Apple workstation can use the optional Metal DOT path.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">ABI reports platform availability, whether native kernels are linked, and whether a Metal pipeline initialized. These fields have different meanings. If the native path is unavailable, the vector-operation implementation retains a CPU fallback with accelerated=false.</p></article><article><h2 id="local-entry-points" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Local entry points</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Run from the ABI checkout with the CLI built and available on PATH. Use disposable data for evaluation; do not connect a test to a live memory store.</p><div class="mt-4"><div class="min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-bg-elevated shadow-border"><div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-border px-4 py-2"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">sh</span><button type="button" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-2 text-2xs text-fg-muted hover:bg-bg-subtle hover:text-fg"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-copy size-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="14" height="14" x="8" y="8" rx="2" ry="2"></rect><path d="M4 16c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V4c0-1.1.9-2 2-2h10c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2"></path></svg>Copy</button></div><pre tabindex="0" class="max-w-full overflow-x-auto p-5 font-mono text-xs leading-7 text-fg"><code>abi backends
+abi wdbx gpu info</code></pre></div></div></article><article><h2 id="acceptance-and-limits" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Acceptance and limits</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Inspect backend status on the intended machine and compare native and fallback results. Publish latency or throughput only with a reproducible harness, workload, hardware and methodology.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">CUDA and Vulkan dispatch are not linked in the inspected ABI GPU implementation.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A compiled kernel is not proof of acceleration on a particular machine or workload.</p></article><article><h2 id="interpret-the-report-correctly" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Interpret the report correctly</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">available describes platform availability, native_kernels describes linkage and accelerated describes an initialized native path. On macOS, Metal can be the preferred backend while accelerated remains false. CUDA and Vulkan names are catalog entries in this implementation, not working native dispatch. Preserve the reported fallback message in an evaluation log so results from different machines are not silently combined.</p></article><article><h2 id="check-native-and-fallback-parity" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Check native and fallback parity</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Run the crate’s vector-operation tests from the ABI checkout using its pinned toolchain wrapper. The following command runs local tests and redirects stdin; it does not publish benchmark results. Review skips and backend initialization failures explicitly. For performance work, add a separately reviewed harness that declares vector dimensions, repetition count and timing boundary.</p><div class="mt-4"><div class="min-w-0 overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-bg-elevated shadow-border"><div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-border px-4 py-2"><span class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">sh</span><button type="button" class="inline-flex h-9 items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md px-2 text-2xs text-fg-muted hover:bg-bg-subtle hover:text-fg"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-copy size-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="14" height="14" x="8" y="8" rx="2" ry="2"></rect><path d="M4 16c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V4c0-1.1.9-2 2-2h10c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2"></path></svg>Copy</button></div><pre tabindex="0" class="max-w-full overflow-x-auto p-5 font-mono text-xs leading-7 text-fg"><code>./tools/cargo.sh test -p abi-gpu &lt; /dev/null</code></pre></div></div></article><article><h2 id="acceptance-for-an-integration" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Acceptance for an integration</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Use equal-length, empty and zero-norm vectors as appropriate to the operation, plus lengths that exercise a remainder beyond a SIMD block. Compare results under a declared numeric tolerance; matching output is a correctness observation, not a speedup. Check the exact caller path because backend status alone does not prove that a particular operation dispatched to the GPU. Record the source revision, machine and backend report with any local result. No hardware-specific speed or power outcome is supplied by this guide.</p></article></div><h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Limitations</h3><div class="mt-3"><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">CUDA and Vulkan dispatch are not linked in the inspected ABI GPU implementation.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">A compiled kernel is not proof of acceleration on a particular machine or workload.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Supporting sources</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">GPU capability reporting and vector operations</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Optional Metal DOT kernel</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li></ul></div></div><div class="mt-12 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">More on this track</h3><ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/gpu-overview">GPU &amp; compute</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/latency-budgets-real-time-orchestration">Latency Budgets for Real-Time AI Orchestration</a></li></ul></div><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Nested implementations</h3><ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li></ul></div></di