l></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">GPU &amp; compute</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/gpu-overview">GPU &amp; compute</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/latency-budgets-real-time-orchestration">Latency Budgets for Real-Time AI Orchestration</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/gpu-implementation-guide">Evaluating Metal acceleration and CPU fallback</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">MCP integrations</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-overview">MCP integrations</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-implementation-guide">Connecting an MCP client to ABI</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">TUI &amp; operator tools</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-overview">TUI &amp; operator tools</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-implementation-guide">Using the local diagnostics dashboard and agent REPL</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-6"><a class="text-xs text-fg-subtle no-underline hover:text-fg active" href="/research/implementations" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Implementations</a><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li><li><a aria-current="page" class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors bg-primary/10 text-fg active" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports" data-status="active">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground">AI</span><span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground">WDBX</span></div><div class="mt-8"><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="validated-public-records" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Validated public records</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Before export, the pipeline parses every research record through its schema, rejects duplicate slugs, and checks public citations for HTTPS URLs that are not localhost. Public PDF paths are constrained to the research download namespace.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The export projects only stable public fields into a versioned index. Internal rendering details do not become accidental API surface, and canonical publication URLs are rooted at the configured MLAI origin.</p></article><article><h2 id="reproducible-artifacts" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Reproducible artifacts</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The exporter writes machine-readable JSON and static HTML, verifies each declared attachment against its expected digest before copying it, and produces a manifest containing publication metadata plus hashes for exported files. It does not generate the PDF attachments it packages.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Digest and manifest generation strengthen provenance by connecting a public artifact to a specific validated content projection. They complement, rather than replace, the revision-pinned citations attached to each research record.</p></article></div></div><h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Limitations</h3><div class="mt-3"><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">A valid URL and pinned revision establish traceability, not independent peer review, experimental replication, or the truth of every claim in the cited source.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">A deterministic export proves reproducible transformation of its inputs; it does not prove that the deployed site currently serves the same artifacts.</li></ul></div><ul class="mt-8 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/developers">Research export validation and stable projection</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">73721dba44afd14a081150a020127a7dec1dbb9e</p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/developers">Research artifact export script</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">73721dba44afd14a081150a020127a7dec1dbb9e</p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/developers">Research content inventory</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">73721dba44afd14a081150a020127a7dec1dbb9e</p></li></ul><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent active" href="/research/implementations" data-status="active" aria-current="page">All implementations</a><a class="text-fg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></div></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disa