ide lucide-sun absolute inset-0 size-4 transition-[opacity,transform,filter] duration-250 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1)] scale-[0.25] opacity-0 blur-[4px]" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"></circle><path d="M12 2v2"></path><path d="M12 20v2"></path><path d="m4.93 4.93 1.41 1.41"></path><path d="m17.66 17.66 1.41 1.41"></path><path d="M2 12h2"></path><path d="M20 12h2"></path><path d="m6.34 17.66-1.41 1.41"></path><path d="m19.07 4.93-1.41 1.41"></path></svg><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-moon absolute inset-0 size-4 transition-[opacity,transform,filter] duration-250 ease-[cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1)] scale-100 opacity-100 blur-0" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20.985 12.486a9 9 0 1 1-9.473-9.472c.405-.022.617.46.402.803a6 6 0 0 0 8.268 8.268c.344-.215.825-.004.803.401"></path></svg></span></button><button type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" class="inline-flex size-11 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-fg lg:hidden" data-overlay-trigger="menu"><span class="sr-only">Open menu</span><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-menu size-5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16"></path><path d="M4 12h16"></path><path d="M4 19h16"></path></svg></button></div></div></header><main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="flex-1"><!--$--><div class="border-b border-border"><div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 pt-16 pb-14 sm:px-6 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-20"><p class="eyebrow">Research · implementations</p><h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-display text-4xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight text-fg sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">What the repositories actually contain.</h1><p class="mt-6 max-w-[62ch] text-lg leading-8 text-fg-muted">Seven nested readings. Each one stays inside a source revision and says what that source does not prove.</p></div></div><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><div class="grid gap-4"><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx · sea · gpu · mcp · tui<!-- --> · <!-- -->1<!-- --> sources</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Quesar organizes interface, orchestration, retrieval, acceleration, storage, and audit as distinct layers so that evidence and runtime claims can be traced to the component that actually supports them.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx<!-- --> · <!-- -->3<!-- --> sources</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The private Quesar application implements bounded ingestion, workspace-scoped extraction and search, and consent-gated model access while making degraded retrieval behavior visible instead of silently changing providers.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx<!-- --> · <!-- -->3<!-- --> sources</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The Quesar mobile Vault keeps one CRUD contract while selecting either the user&#x27;s private CloudKit database or an encrypted local SecureStore fallback and exposing the selected backend to the application.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · mcp · tui<!-- --> · <!-- -->3<!-- --> sources</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Quasar couples an Anthropic tool loop to a narrowly constrained project filesystem, producing a local application through inspectable read, list, and write operations rather than granting an unconstrained shell.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx · sea · gpu · mcp · tui<!-- --> · <!-- -->3<!-- --> sources</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Abbey centralizes capability statements in a typed registry whose status, evidence, dependencies, feature flags, and refusal behavior can be projected into documentation and checked for drift.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx · sea · gpu · mcp · tui<!-- --> · <!-- -->0<!-- --> sources</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">WDBX Specimen combines a provenance-aware architecture specification with explicit browser and native runtime profiles, then uses conformance tests to make a bounded subset of the design executable.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx<!-- --> · <!-- -->3<!-- --> sources</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The Quesar research export pipeline converts validated publication records into stable JSON and static HTML, verifies and copies declared attachments, and records content digests while enforcing unique identifiers, public source URLs, and canonical links.</p></article></a></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm active" href="/research" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Research index</a></div></section><script>(function(a,f){let l;try{l=JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(a)||"{}")}catch{return}const n=l?.[f||history.state?.__TSR_key];let c=!1;for(const t in n){const e=n[t],o=e?.scrollX,s=e?.scrollY;if(Number.isFinite(o)&&Number.isFinite(s)){if(t==="window")scrollTo(o,s),c=!0;else if(t)try{const r=document.querySelector(t);r&&(r.scrollLeft=o,r.scrollTop=s)}catch{}}}if(c)return;const i=location.hash.slice(1);if(i){const t=history.state?.__hashScrollIntoViewOptions??!0;if(t){const e=document.getElementById(i);e&&e.scrollIntoView(t)}return}scrollTo(0,0)})("tsr-scroll-restoration-v1_3");document.currentScript.remove()</script><!--/$--></main><footer class="mt-auto"><div c