ounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a aria-current="page" class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors bg-primary/10 text-fg active" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance" data-status="active">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground">AI</span><span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground">WDBX</span><span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground">SEA</span><span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground">GPU</span><span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground">MCP</span><span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 font-mono text-2xs text-muted-foreground">TUI</span></div><div class="mt-8"><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="specification-with-provenance" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Specification with provenance</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The architecture specification separates source-backed statements, recommended design choices, and open questions. It also maintains a contradiction register and contributor provenance so unresolved design tension remains visible instead of being flattened into one apparently settled narrative.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Acceptance cases are written as requirements for an implementation, not retroactive proof that every requirement is already satisfied. That distinction makes the document useful as both an architectural map and a research agenda.</p></article><article><h2 id="two-honest-runtime-profiles" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Two honest runtime profiles</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The browser profile emphasizes deterministic prompt features and seeded sampling without claiming online weight training or learned generation. The native profile documents an initial Rust implementation whose lexical processing and persistence behavior are narrower than unrestricted semantic intelligence.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Native conformance tests exercise the implemented profile. Together, the profiles show how one specification can support multiple runtimes while requiring each runtime to state exactly which semantics and proofs it provides.</p></article></div></div><h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Limitations</h3><div class="mt-3"><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Source citations are withheld because the underlying repository is private and cannot be verified by public readers.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">WDBX Specimen is an independent design-and-conformance project, not evidence for every capability of the canonical WDBX storage substrate.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Specification requirements, browser demonstrations, native conformance, performance measurements, and production readiness are separate evidence layers.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent active" href="/research/implementations" data-status="active" aria-current="page">All implementations</a><a class="text-fg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a><a class="text-fg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></div></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px