aluate assistant workflows with explicit behavior, provider and review boundaries.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/gpu-implementation-guide"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE<!-- --> · <!-- -->implementation guide<!-- --> · <!-- -->Implemented<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->SEPTEMBER 2026<!-- --> · <!-- -->2 min read</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">Evaluating Metal acceleration and CPU fallback</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Assess whether a target Apple workstation can use the optional Metal DOT path.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/mcp-implementation-guide"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE<!-- --> · <!-- -->implementation guide<!-- --> · <!-- -->Implemented<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->SEPTEMBER 2026<!-- --> · <!-- -->3 min read</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">Connecting an MCP client to ABI</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Evaluate a local integration from an MCP client into the ABI tool catalog.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/tui-implementation-guide"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover"><p class="text-xs text-accent">IMPLEMENTATION GUIDE<!-- --> · <!-- -->implementation guide<!-- --> · <!-- -->Implemented<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->SEPTEMBER 2026<!-- --> · <!-- -->2 min read</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">Using the local diagnostics dashboard and agent REPL</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Give developers a local diagnostics and interaction surface during evaluation.</p></article></a></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Implementations</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Nested cases. Each one names the source it depends on.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">These sit under /research/implementations. They are implementation readings, not extra benchmark claims.</p></header><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx · sea · gpu · mcp · tui</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Quesar organizes interface, orchestration, retrieval, acceleration, storage, and audit as distinct layers so that evidence and runtime claims can be traced to the component that actually supports them.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The private Quesar application implements bounded ingestion, workspace-scoped extraction and search, and consent-gated model access while making degraded retrieval behavior visible instead of silently changing providers.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The Quesar mobile Vault keeps one CRUD contract while selecting either the user&#x27;s private CloudKit database or an encrypted local SecureStore fallback and exposing the selected backend to the application.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · mcp · tui</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Quasar couples an Anthropic tool loop to a narrowly constrained project filesystem, producing a local application through inspectable read, list, and write operations rather than granting an unconstrained shell.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx · sea · gpu · mcp · tui</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Abbey centralizes capability statements in a typed registry whose status, evidence, dependencies, feature flags, and refusal behavior can be projected into documentation and checked for drift.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><p class="text-xs text-accent">ai · wdbx · sea · gpu · mcp · tui</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">WDBX Specimen combines a provenance-aware architecture specification with explicit browser and native runtime profiles, then uses conformance tests to make a bounded subset of the design executable.</p></article></a><a class="no-underline" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 surface-hover h-full"><p clas