ext-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/gpu-implementation-guide">Evaluating Metal acceleration and CPU fallback</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">MCP integrations</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-overview">MCP integrations</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-implementation-guide">Connecting an MCP client to ABI</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">TUI &amp; operator tools</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-overview">TUI &amp; operator tools</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-implementation-guide">Using the local diagnostics dashboard and agent REPL</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-6"><a class="text-xs text-fg-subtle no-underline hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations">Implementations</a><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="mb-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Practical summary</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Evaluate assistant workflows with explicit behavior, provider and review boundaries.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Status</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">The described source behavior is implemented; customer outcomes and deployment readiness are not established.</p><p class="mt-2 font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">Reviewed <!-- -->2026-09-30</p></article></div><nav aria-label="Related products" class="mb-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent" href="/products">All products</a></nav><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="practical-context" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Practical context</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A corrected account of deterministic local profile routing and adaptive state in the SEA path.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Evaluate assistant workflows with explicit behavior, provider and review boundaries.</p></article><article><h2 id="implementation-and-research-boundary" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Implementation and research boundary</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Base local completion selects a persona from keyword-derived signals and renders a template. The adaptive completion function can use persisted router weights when invoked through the SEA learning path. The learning loop owns persistence of the updated state.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">This note does not claim a learned classifier of emotions, confidence-thresholded response blending, historical task-fit retrieval or a complete automatic rerouting audit trail. Those broader claims in the historical edition are not established by the cited implementation.</p></article><article><h2 id="base-route-additive-keyword-weights" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Base route: additive keyword weights</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The canonical prior is Abbey 0.40, Aviva 0.30 and ABI 0.30. The router splits ASCII whitespace, trims selected trailing punctuation and applies case-insensitive prefix matches against its keyword table. Each match adds one tenth of the keyword’s persona score. A positive total is normalized, then the largest weight wins; ties prefer Abbey, then Aviva, then ABI. These values describe a deterministic heuristic, not a trained probability model.</p><div class="mt-4 space-y-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 px-4 py-3 text-fg"><div tabindex="0" class="my-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-subtle px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">w^{(0)}=(0.40,0.30,0.30)</div><div tabindex="0" class="my-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-subtle px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">\widetilde{w}_p=w^{(0)}_p+0.1\sum_{k\in\mathrm{matches}(I)}s_{k,p}</div><div tabindex="0" class="my-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-subtle px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">w_p=\frac{\widetilde{w}_p}{\sum_j\widetilde{w}_j}</div></div></article><article><h2 id="explicit-selection-and-adaptive-state" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Explicit selection and adaptive state</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">An exact leading persona address can override keyword routing. The parser accepts forms such as “Aviva, be direct” or “ABI: orchestrate”; mentioning a persona later in prose is different. In the adaptive path, the pure modulator updates an exponential moving average and renormalizes it. The default smoothing factor is 0.3. Serialization and validation are explicit; malformed persisted state falls back to defaults rather than becoming an arbitrary routing distribution.</p><div class="mt-4 space-y-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 px-4 py-3 text-fg"><div tabindex="0" class="my-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-subtle px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">e_t=\mathrm{normalize}\left(0.3w_t+0.7e_{t-1}\right)</div></div></article><article><h2 id="what-to-test-and-what-the-result-means" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">What to test and what the result means</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Test neutral text, each explicit address, punctuation and whitespace variants, near ties and corrupted saved state. Keep the original utterance separate from retrieved context so evidence text cannot silently impersonate the user’s persona selector. The SEA loop owns loading and saving adaptive state; base completion remains store-independent. Compare selected profiles and returned outputs across repeated runs at the pinned revision. A deterministic match establishes routing behavior, not empathy, expertise, calibrated uncertainty or automatic text blending between separate models.</p></article><article><h2 id="evaluation-before-adoption" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Evaluation before adoption</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">For a customer pilot, choose a concrete task and identify whether it uses local templates or an explicitly configured provider. Evaluate task correctness, escalation and data handling with representative inputs before making quality claims.</p></article></div><h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Limitations</h3><div class="mt-3"><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Local completion renders persona templates; it is not evidence of a trained foundation model.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Keyword-based checks cannot establish general safety or emotional understanding.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">This note does not claim a learned classifier of emotions, confidence-thresholded response blending, historical task-fit retrieval or a complete automatic rerouting audit trail. Those broader claims in the historical edition are not established by the cited implementation.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Supporting sources</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Local completion and adaptive routing</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Deterministic persona router</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Learning loop and persisted router weights</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">EMA update and state validation</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Canonical persona priors</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li></ul></div><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Downloads</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a href="/research/multi-persona-routing-policy-weights-2026-09-06.pdf" download="" class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline">Corrected source-audited PDF · 2026-09-06<!-- --> (PDF)</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">Current edition<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->2026-09-06<!-- --> · <!-- -->3<!-- --> pages</p><p class="mt-1 break-all font-mono text-2xs text-