ter rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/sparse-evidence-attention-context-assembly">Sparse Evidence Attention for Bounded Context Assembly</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/backtrace-confidence-signals-hallucination">Backtrace Confidence Signals for Hallucination Reduction</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/chunk-provenance-long-context-retrieval">Chunk Provenance in Long-Context Retrieval Systems</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">GPU &amp; compute</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/gpu-overview">GPU &amp; compute</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/latency-budgets-real-time-orchestration">Latency Budgets for Real-Time AI Orchestration</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/gpu-implementation-guide">Evaluating Metal acceleration and CPU fallback</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">MCP integrations</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-overview">MCP integrations</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-implementation-guide">Connecting an MCP client to ABI</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">TUI &amp; operator tools</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-overview">TUI &amp; operator tools</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-implementation-guide">Using the local diagnostics dashboard and agent REPL</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-6"><a class="text-xs text-fg-subtle no-underline hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations">Implementations</a><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="mb-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Practical summary</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Evaluate assistant workflows with explicit behavior, provider and review boundaries.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Status</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">The described source behavior is implemented; customer outcomes and deployment readiness are not established.</p><p class="mt-2 font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">Reviewed <!-- -->2026-09-30</p></article></div><nav aria-label="Related products" class="mb-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent" href="/products">All products</a></nav><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="practical-context" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Practical context</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A bounded description of local deterministic processing and its evaluation uses.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Evaluate assistant workflows with explicit behavior, provider and review boundaries.</p></article><article><h2 id="implementation-and-research-boundary" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Implementation and research boundary</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Local ABI completion renders in-process persona templates, and the evidence path can read a configured local store. Vector operations retain a CPU fallback when native acceleration is unavailable. This supports self-contained functional experiments with synthetic inputs.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">This is not a claim that every product feature works offline or that sensitive data is protected automatically. Provider calls, application logging, permissions and retention require their own data-flow review.</p></article><article><h2 id="define-the-offline-boundary" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Define the offline boundary</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Offline can refer to generation, retrieval, interface rendering or storage, and those are not interchangeable. The local ABI completion function does not invoke the named provider model: it generates deterministic persona text. SEA can assemble evidence from a configured durable store, and CPU vector computation can support functional experiments when native acceleration is unavailable. These paths make useful local fixtures, but their successful execution cannot certify every integration as offline.</p></article><article><h2 id="a-safe-evaluation-setup" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">A safe evaluation setup</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Use synthetic prompts and a disposable data directory, record the selected completion mode and backend report, and keep provider credentials outside the test environment. Inspect the intended entry point for persistence before running it. For a retrieval experiment, populate the scratch corpus with known records and verify that output context derives from those records. Compare a run with no stored evidence and a run with relevant or contradictory evidence; do not describe the difference as quality improvement without a rubric.</p></article><article><h2 id="privacy-and-acceptance" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Privacy and acceptance</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Trace inputs, generated output, logs, caches and exports across the whole application. A local model can still be embedded in software that transmits telemetry or calls remote tools. Inspect those paths and verify network behavior in the intended environment before making an offline claim. Evaluate access controls and deletion separately from physical locality. A partner can use this boundary map to choose what may remain on a workstation, while recognizing that production model capability, sensitive-data handling and operational support each require their own acceptance evidence.</p></article><article><h2 id="evaluation-before-adoption" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Evaluation before adoption</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">For a customer pilot, choose a concrete task and identify whether it uses local templates or an explicitly configured provider. Evaluate task correctness, escalation and data handling with representative inputs before making quality claims.</p></article></div><h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Limitations</h3><div class="mt-3"><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Local completion renders persona templates; it is not evidence of a trained foundation model.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Keyword-based checks cannot establish general safety or emotional understanding.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">This is not a claim that every product feature works offline or that sensitive data is protected automatically. Provider calls, application logging, permissions and retention require their own data-flow review.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Supporting sources</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Local completion and adaptive routing</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">Bounded evidence recall and prompt assembly</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/abi">GPU capability reporting and vector operations</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">80dfe079ebe7413a6815c2d564be1f0aaa901267</code></p></li></ul></div></div><div class="mt-12 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">More on this track</h3><ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/ai-overview">AI &amp; agent behavior</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/policy-locked-tool-use-multi-agent">Policy-Locked Tool Use in Multi-Agent Systems</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/human-approval-gates-operators-use">Human Approval Gates That Operators Actually Use</a></li></ul></div><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Nested implementations</h3><ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-u