rline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/mcp-implementation-guide">Connecting an MCP client to ABI</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-5"><p class="text-xs text-fg-subtle">TUI &amp; operator tools</p><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-overview">TUI &amp; operator tools</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/tui-implementation-guide">Using the local diagnostics dashboard and agent REPL</a></li></ul></div><div class="mt-6"><a class="text-xs text-fg-subtle no-underline hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations">Implementations</a><ul class="mt-2 space-y-0.5"><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="mb-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Practical summary</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Build document recall and decision-history prototypes with explicit source ownership.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Status</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">The described source behavior is implemented; customer outcomes and deployment readiness are not established.</p><p class="mt-2 font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">Reviewed <!-- -->2026-09-30</p></article></div><nav aria-label="Related products" class="mb-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent" href="/products/wdbx">Explore <!-- -->WDBX</a><a class="text-accent" href="/products">All products</a></nav><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="practical-context" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Practical context</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Inspect how a candidate ranking can expose the factors that influenced it.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Build document recall and decision-history prototypes with explicit source ownership.</p></article><article><h2 id="implementation-and-research-boundary" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Implementation and research boundary</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The hybrid retrieval API first obtains vector candidates and then applies graph and caller-provided persona factors. Ranked results include observable score components alongside the borrowed vector and stable identifier.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A ranking factor can explain an ordering without proving a source is true. The caller supplies graph context and persona affinity; the library does not establish that an application captured a complete causal history.</p></article><article><h2 id="representing-relationships-without-overstating-them" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Representing relationships without overstating them</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A retrieval graph supplies record identifiers, timestamps and adjacency to the ranking layer. The temporal module builds an undirected reachability view from persisted causal records. This is useful for finding nearby context, but it deliberately loses the directional distinction needed for a causal explanation. A product should display the actual relationship available, such as proximity to a selected record, rather than relabel every edge as established causation.</p></article><article><h2 id="weight-behavior-and-a-worked-example" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Weight behavior and a worked example</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">For a reachable record at h hops, causal weight is the larger of a floor and decay raised to h. Default decay is 0.6 and floor is 0.25. A one-hop record receives 0.6, a two-hop record 0.36, and a three-hop record the floor because 0.216 is smaller. Missing reachability within the bounded search also returns the floor. These arithmetic examples explain the function; they are not measured retrieval-quality results.</p><div class="mt-4 space-y-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 px-4 py-3 text-fg"><div tabindex="0" class="my-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-subtle px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">\gamma(h)=\max(c_{\mathrm{floor}},c_{\mathrm{decay}}^h)</div></div></article><article><h2 id="evaluate-factors-and-ranking-stability" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Evaluate factors and ranking stability</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Construct equal-semantic candidates with different timestamps, reachability and persona factors so each influence can be isolated. Keep the original candidate set when comparing two weighting policies; otherwise a change in approximate search can be mistaken for a reranking effect. Record the complete factors and final order, including missing-node cases. Test zero persona affinity and stale records, because multiplying factors can suppress a semantically strong candidate. A decision-review interface should let the reviewer inspect the underlying source rather than treating a high combined score as an endorsement.</p></article><article><h2 id="evaluation-before-adoption" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Evaluation before adoption</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Start with a synthetic or authorized corpus. Check recovery, source identifiers, update behavior and retrieval relevance. Treat application permissions, data retention and deployment evidence as additional requirements.</p></article></div><h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Limitations</h3><div class="mt-3"><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Storage integrity establishes consistency, not the truth of stored statements.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">The reference cluster protocol does not establish production multi-host operation or sharding.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">A ranking factor can explain an ordering without proving a source is true. The caller supplies graph context and persona affinity; the library does not establish that an application captured a complete causal history.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Supporting sources</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Hybrid retrieval and observable score factors</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Layered HNSW index</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Temporal and causal ranking functions</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li></ul></div></div><div class="mt-12 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">More on this track</h3><ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/wdbx-overview">WDBX memory &amp; retrieval</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/wdbx-weighted-backtrace-memory-store">WDBX: 