implementations/six-layer-evidence-aware-platform">A six-layer architecture for evidence-aware AI systems</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/private-document-intelligence-pipeline">A private document pipeline with explicit fallback behavior</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/mobile-vault-cloudkit-local-fallback">Mobile Vault persistence across CloudKit and local fallback</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/quasar-bounded-repository-generation">Quasar as a bounded repository-generation loop</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/abbey-executable-capability-ledger">Abbey capability claims as an executable ledger</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/wdbx-specimen-architecture-and-conformance">WDBX Specimen separates architecture, runtime profiles, and proof</a></li><li><a class="flex min-h-10 items-center rounded-md px-2 text-sm no-underline transition-colors text-fg-muted hover:bg-muted hover:text-fg" href="/research/implementations/deterministic-research-provenance-exports">Deterministic research exports with citation gates</a></li></ul></div></nav><div><div class="mb-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Practical summary</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Build document recall and decision-history prototypes with explicit source ownership.</p></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Status</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">The described source behavior is implemented; customer outcomes and deployment readiness are not established.</p><p class="mt-2 font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">Reviewed <!-- -->2026-09-30</p></article></div><nav aria-label="Related products" class="mb-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm"><a class="text-accent" href="/products/wdbx">Explore <!-- -->WDBX</a><a class="text-accent" href="/products">All products</a></nav><div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10"><article><h2 id="practical-context" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Practical context</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">A technical note on durable storage, approximate vector search and inspectable ranking, with legacy and canonical episode paths distinguished.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Build document recall and decision-history prototypes with explicit source ownership.</p></article><article><h2 id="implementation-and-research-boundary" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Implementation and research boundary</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The active Rust substrate provides durable snapshots and WAL recovery, a layered HNSW graph, and a hybrid retrieval API that exposes score components. HNSW defaults in the inspected source are M=16, EF_CONSTRUCTION=40 and EF_SEARCH=32.</p><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Legacy snapshot chain verification and strict content verification are different entry points. Canonical v3 episode storage is also a distinct API. Applications must identify the path they actually use; this note does not assert that every write from every consumer passed episode admission.</p></article><article><h2 id="similarity-and-approximate-candidate-selection" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Similarity and approximate candidate selection</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">For nonzero, equal-dimension vectors, cosine similarity is the normalized dot product below. It ranges from -1 to 1; it is not a probability. The CPU reference returns zero for empty or zero-norm inputs. HNSW supplies approximate candidates rather than an exhaustive guarantee of the globally closest records. An evaluation therefore needs an exact-search baseline for its chosen corpus and requested result count.</p><div class="mt-4 space-y-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 px-4 py-3 text-fg"><div tabindex="0" class="my-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-subtle px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">\sigma(q,v)=\frac{\sum_d q_d v_d}{\sqrt{\sum_d q_d^2}\sqrt{\sum_d v_d^2}}</div></div></article><article><h2 id="hybrid-ranking-is-a-separate-calculation" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Hybrid ranking is a separate calculation</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">The hybrid scorer clamps semantic similarity and caller-provided persona affinity to the unit interval, then multiplies them by temporal and causal factors. With a positive half-life, temporal weight halves each half-life of nonnegative age; a nonpositive half-life disables decay. Missing timestamps use the query time. Causal reachability is bounded and uses an undirected view of persisted edges, so a hop count should not be interpreted as a proof of causal direction.</p><div class="mt-4 space-y-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 px-4 py-3 text-fg"><div tabindex="0" class="my-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-subtle px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">S_j=\mathrm{clamp}_{[0,1]}(\sigma_j)\,\tau_j\,\gamma_j\,\mathrm{clamp}_{[0,1]}(\pi_j)</div><div tabindex="0" class="my-1 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-subtle px-5 py-4 font-mono text-xs text-fg-subtle">\tau_j=2^{-\max(0,t_0-t_j)/t_{1/2}}</div></div></article><article><h2 id="a-reconstructible-storage-experiment" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">A reconstructible storage experiment</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Use a disposable corpus with known vector neighbors and explicit metadata. Capture the source revision, vector dimensions, insertion order, query vectors and index parameters. Compare approximate results with exact ranking, then checkpoint, reopen and repeat the same queries. Separately alter a copied block payload to distinguish predecessor-link checks from strict content-hash verification. Neither successful recovery nor matching hashes validates the factual content of a stored statement. Canonical episode commitments must be tested through the v3 episode path, not inferred from legacy snapshot success.</p></article><article><h2 id="evaluation-before-adoption" class="scroll-mt-24 font-display text-[1.65rem] leading-tight tracking-tight text-fg">Evaluation before adoption</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-[66ch] text-base leading-8 text-fg">Start with a synthetic or authorized corpus. Check recovery, source identifiers, update behavior and retrieval relevance. Treat application permissions, data retention and deployment evidence as additional requirements.</p></article></div><h3 class="mt-10 font-display text-xl">Limitations</h3><div class="mt-3"><ul class="grid gap-3 text-sm text-fg-muted sm:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Storage integrity establishes consistency, not the truth of stored statements.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">The reference cluster protocol does not establish production multi-host operation or sharding.</li><li class="surface px-4 py-3">Legacy snapshot chain verification and strict content verification are different entry points. Canonical v3 episode storage is also a distinct API. Applications must identify the path they actually use; this note does not assert that every write from every consumer passed episode admission.</li></ul></div><div class="mt-10 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Supporting sources</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Durable store and writer ownership</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Layered HNSW index</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Hybrid retrieval and observable score factors</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Snapshot chain verification</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Canonical episode persistence</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">Temporal and causal ranking functions</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/wdbx">CPU cosine reference and vector edge cases</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">source<!-- --> · revision<!-- --> <code class="break-all font-mono">e45410356ceb4e96f0dc26a83b02e1c18cf94860</code></p></li></ul></div><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Downloads</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3"><li class="surface p-4"><a href="/research/wdbx-weighted-backtrace-memory-store-2026-09-06.pdf" download="" class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline">Corrected source-audited PDF · 2026-09-06<!-- --> (PDF)</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">Current edition<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->2026-09-06<!-- --> · <!-- -->3<!-- --> pages</p><p class="mt-1 break-all font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">SHA-256: <!-- -->294a7906391b064273691eff60a0f83242cbbb78e2a894321285e993f31f3fa2</p></li><li class="surface p-4"><a href="/research/wdbx-weighted-backtrace-memory-store.pdf" download="" class="text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline hover:underline">Historical June 2026 PDF — superseded<!-- --> (PDF)</a><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-muted">Historical edition<!-- --> ·<!-- --> <!-- -->2026-06-01<!-- --> · <!-- -->5<!-- --> pages</p><p class="mt-1 break-all font-mono text-2xs text-fg-subtle">SHA-256: <!-- -->1030bd50a64ab2426ba6558aee26398cfea1a7b7de39e527db0685bf54a853cf</p></li></ul></div></div><div class="mt-12 grid gap-8"><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">More on this track</h3><ul class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/wdbx-overview">WDBX memory &amp; retrieval</a></li><li><a class="text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/research/w