on class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><p class="max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Engagement scope, deliverables, and acceptance criteria are agreed for each project.</p><a href="https://github.com/donaldfilimon/quesar.cloud/blob/f3ccc082f72ef868ca3c3a60f332f7efe9cfe492/src/lib/mlai/categories/services.ts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm text-accent underline underline-offset-4">Inspect the source behind this page</a></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><div id="engagements" class="scroll-mt-28"><p class="eyebrow">Work with MLAI</p><h2 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Turn your next system into something inspectable.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Start with a defined engineering scope. Agree deliverables, access, and acceptance criteria before work begins.</p><div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2"><article class="rounded-xl border border-accent/40 bg-bg-elevated p-6 sm:p-8"><p class="eyebrow">Pilot engagement</p><h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl tracking-tight">$2,500 <span class="text-base text-fg-muted">USD / one month</span></h3><p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">A scoped engineering engagement for an AI workflow, retrieval path, or private deployment. Scope and delivery dates are agreed with you.</p><ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-sm text-fg-muted"><li>Agreed deliverables and acceptance criteria</li><li>One month, with no automatic renewal</li><li>Invoiced engagement; hosted model access is not included</li></ul><a class="mt-7 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-full bg-accent px-6 text-sm font-medium text-bg" href="/contact?service=Pilot+engineering+engagement">Discuss the Pilot →</a><div class="mt-4"><div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-bg-elevated p-4 " role="note"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Static preview</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Online invoice requests<!-- --> requires the server deployment, which is not live here.</p></div><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Contact us to agree the scope and arrange an invoice. Online payment collection is not available on this site.</p></div></article><article class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-card p-6 sm:p-8"><p class="eyebrow">Platform engagement</p><h3 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl tracking-tight">Built around your scope.</h3><p class="mt-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">For larger integration, hardening, and deployment work, define the architecture and delivery milestones together. Pricing follows the agreed scope.</p><ul class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-sm text-fg-muted"><li>Architecture and integration planning</li><li>Operational and security acceptance criteria</li><li>Custom pricing and invoicing</li></ul><a class="mt-7 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center text-sm font-medium text-accent" href="/contact?service=Platform+engineering+engagement">Discuss a Platform engagement →</a></article></div></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Core</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Nine proposed engagement scopes.</h2></header><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Autonomy Readiness Audit</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: map workflows, prompt surfaces, data paths, and approval gates to identify automation candidates and the evidence needed to evaluate their risks.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Risk register</li><li>Control-map</li><li>90-day rollout plan</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=Autonomy+Readiness+Audit">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">WDBX Retrieval Architecture</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: design retrieval pipelines with source context and inspectable vector search; evaluate weighted backtrace approaches separately.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Index strategy</li><li>Recall benchmarks</li><li>Trace schema</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=WDBX+Retrieval+Architecture">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Multi-Agent Orchestration</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: define and implement agent roles, tool permissions, task handoffs, and conflict-resolution policies against agreed acceptance criteria.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Agent graph</li><li>Tool policy</li><li>Evaluation harness</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=Multi-Agent+Orchestration">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Model &amp; Runtime Optimization</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: profile inference paths, memory pressure, batching, and edge constraints on an agreed workload and environment.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Latency profile</li><li>Optimization backlog</li><li>Capacity model</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=Model+%26+Runtime+Optimization">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Safety &amp; Compliance Layering</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: develop policy checks, audit trails, and red-team scenarios for an agreed system boundary. Legal or compliance acceptance requires separate review.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Policy matrix</li><li>Audit events</li><li>Red-team scripts</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=Safety+%26+Compliance+Layering">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Private AI Deployment</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: assess and package workflows for an agreed VPC, on-premise, offline, or hybrid deployment boundary.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Deployment topology</li><li>Runbook</li><li>Rollback plan</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=Private+AI+Deployment">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Research Translation</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: translate papers and notebooks into a constrained prototype, API contract, and test plan.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Prototype hardening</li><li>API contract</li><li>Test plan</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=Research+Translation">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Executive &amp; Engineering Workshops</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: run workshops with leadership, security, product, and engineering to document autonomy decisions and risk boundaries.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Decision memo</li><li>Team training</li><li>Architecture review</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=Executive+%26+Engineering+Workshops">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="surface accent-edge p-6 flex h-full flex-col"><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Continuous Evaluation Systems</h3><p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed scope: build evaluation suites for tool use, retrieval faithfulness, policy behavior, and regression drift against agreed criteria.</p><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted"><li>Eval suite</li><li>Scorecards</li><li>Release gates</li></ul><a class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-t border-border pt-4 text-sm text-accent no-underline hover:underline" href="/contact?service=Continuous+Evaluation+Systems">Discuss this service <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Proposed engagement process</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">Define the release evidence together.</h2><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-muted sm:text-lg">These four proposed phases identify deliverables to agree for each project: a register, a harness, a baseline, and acceptance criteria.</p></header><ol class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">01</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Audit</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed deliverable: an inventory of workflows, data, tools, and failure modes, with a risk register for review before design.</p></div></li><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">02</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Design</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed deliverables: a bounded architecture for retrieval, permissions, personas, and deployment, plus an agreed evaluation harness.</p></div></li><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">03</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Build</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed deliverables: an implementation on agreed operator-owned hardware and a baseline the team can rerun against the harness.</p></div></li><li class="surface flex gap-4 p-5"><span class="flex size-9 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-bg font-mono text-2xs text-accent shadow-border">04</span><div><h3 class="font-display text-xl">Harden</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed deliverables: red-team checks, rollback guidance, observability, operator training, and a release gate with explicit acceptance criteria.</p></div></li></ol></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28"><header class="mb-12 max-w-3xl"><p class="eyebrow">Fit</p><h2 class="section-title mt-4 text-fg">What we say no to.</h2></header><div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2"><aside class="surface accent-edge p-5 [--edge:var(--accent)]"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Scope discipline</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed engagement boundary: agree who may access the corpus, where it may move, and which provider calls require approval before implementation.</p></aside><aside class="surface accent-edge p-5 [--edge:var(--accent)]"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Claims discipline</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">Proposed evidence requirement: deliverables should tag figures as targets, source reports, or measurements. Measurements require an agreed workload, environment, and reproduction record.</p></aside></div><div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm" href="/contact">Discuss your project</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px border-border bg-card/80 text-foreground hover:bg-muted h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm" href="/architecture">Read the architecture</a></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6"><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border border-transparent font-medium whitespace-nowrap no-underline transition-[background-color,color,box-shadow,opacity,transform] duration-150 ease-out select-none focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-ring disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 active:not-disabled:translate-y-px bg-primary text-primary-foreground hover:bg-primary/80 h-11 rounded-md px-4 text-sm" href="/contact">Discuss your project</a></div><div class="mt-10"><div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2"><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/developers"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Developers</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">What you can run without an engagement.</p></a><a class="surface surface-hover p-5 no-underline" href="/company"><p class="text-xs text-accent">Next</p><h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl text-fg">Company</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-fg-muted">Who develops this, and the site&#x27;s integrity rules.</p></a></div></div></section><script>(function(a,f){let l;try{l=JSON.parse(sessionStorage.getItem(a)||"{}")}catch{return}const n=l?.[f||history.state?.__TSR_key];let c=!1;for(const t in n){const e=n[t],o=e?.scrollX,s=e?.scrollY;if(Number.isFinite(o)&&Number.isFinite(s)){if(t==="window")scrollTo(o,s),c=!0;else if(t)try{const r=document.querySelector(t);r&&(r.scrollLeft=o,r.scrollTop=s)}catch{}}}if(c)return;const i=location.hash.slice(1);if(i){const t=history.state?.__hashScrollIntoViewOptions??!0;if(t){const e=document.getElementById(i);e&&e.scrollIntoView(t)}return}scrollTo(0,0)})("tsr-scroll-restoration-v1_3");document.currentScript.remove()</script><!--/$--></main><footer class="mt-